1
00:00:04,943 --> 00:00:07,177
(mellow jazz music playing)

2
00:00:10,406 --> 00:00:12,907
♪ ♪

3
00:00:41,834 --> 00:00:43,300
SNAKE:
<i>Stop.</i>

4
00:00:43,436 --> 00:00:45,071
WOLF:<i> I'll stop if you just</i>
<i>explain it to me,</i>

5
00:00:45,207 --> 00:00:46,643
<i>-because I don't...</i>
<i>-Would you please just drop it?</i>

6
00:00:46,778 --> 00:00:48,114
WOLF: All right, all right,
fine, fine, fine, fine.

7
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:49,245
Consider it dropped.
It's dropped.

8
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:51,373
-It's on the ground.
-Good.

9
00:00:52,376 --> 00:00:54,251
But, I mean, come on,
everybody loves birthdays.

10
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:56,112
-(groans)
-You got decorations.

11
00:00:56,248 --> 00:00:58,121
You got balloons.
You got parties and cake.

12
00:00:58,256 --> 00:00:59,755
Look, I don't need presents,

13
00:00:59,891 --> 00:01:02,886
I don't want decorations,
and I'm-I'm not a cake guy.

14
00:01:03,022 --> 00:01:04,853
Seriously, though,
you don't like cake?

15
00:01:04,988 --> 00:01:06,862
Name one food better than cake.

16
00:01:06,997 --> 00:01:08,130
Guinea pig.

17
00:01:08,266 --> 00:01:09,993
Oh, again with the guinea pig.

18
00:01:10,128 --> 00:01:12,061
(chuckling):
I bet if I blindfolded you,

19
00:01:12,196 --> 00:01:13,896
you wouldn't be able
to tell the difference

20
00:01:14,031 --> 00:01:15,866
between a skunk
and a guinea pig.

21
00:01:16,001 --> 00:01:18,668
Wrong. Snakes have
impeccable taste buds.

22
00:01:18,803 --> 00:01:20,809
-I can taste air.
-Air?

23
00:01:20,944 --> 00:01:22,437
Yes. Air.

24
00:01:22,572 --> 00:01:23,746
(slurping)

25
00:01:23,881 --> 00:01:25,412
Mm. Nice.

26
00:01:25,548 --> 00:01:27,709
I don't know.
They're a little, uh...

27
00:01:27,844 --> 00:01:29,383
a little cute for my taste.

28
00:01:29,518 --> 00:01:31,712
That's what makes them
so delicious.

29
00:01:31,847 --> 00:01:33,615
You're not just eating food.

30
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,483
You're eating pure goodness.

31
00:01:35,619 --> 00:01:37,052
It's not about the pig.

32
00:01:37,187 --> 00:01:40,560
It's about what it symbolizes
on a deeper level.

33
00:01:41,892 --> 00:01:43,263
So, you can...
you can taste air?

34
00:01:43,398 --> 00:01:44,659
-(groans)
-What else you got?

35
00:01:44,795 --> 00:01:45,959
-Forget about it.
-W-W-Wait.

36
00:01:46,094 --> 00:01:47,668
-Can you also hear color?
-(groans)

37
00:01:47,803 --> 00:01:49,669
-(chuckles) Can you see sound?
-All right, all right. Okay.

38
00:01:49,805 --> 00:01:51,865
'Cause we should really be
capitalizing on these skills.

39
00:01:52,001 --> 00:01:53,735
Okay, all right, fine.
Get it all out.

40
00:01:53,871 --> 00:01:55,076
-Get it all out now.
-Okay, okay.

41
00:01:55,211 --> 00:01:56,667
-(retches)
-(alarm bell dings)

42
00:01:56,803 --> 00:01:58,379
Look at that. 4:00 p.m.

43
00:01:58,514 --> 00:02:00,747
Now I know the exact moment
our friendship died.

44
00:02:00,883 --> 00:02:02,708
(Wolf laughs)

45
00:02:02,843 --> 00:02:04,584
-Let's bounce.
-Yep.

46
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:09,146
Tastes like, um, you're gonna
stick me with the bill-- again.

47
00:02:09,282 --> 00:02:11,047
-(people gasping)
-Well, it is my birthday.

48
00:02:11,182 --> 00:02:12,851
So now you play
the birthday card?

49
00:02:12,987 --> 00:02:14,691
-That's interesting.
-(chuckling)

50
00:02:14,826 --> 00:02:18,129
Can we get a check, please,
when you get a chance?

51
00:02:18,264 --> 00:02:21,164
Hello? Checkity-check-check.

52
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:22,797
-You know what?
-(screams)

53
00:02:22,932 --> 00:02:26,229
We're just gonna leave
the money right here, okay?

54
00:02:26,364 --> 00:02:28,098
You know the one good thing
about this place?

55
00:02:28,233 --> 00:02:30,008
-What? -We never have to wait
for a table.

56
00:02:30,144 --> 00:02:31,442
Well, isn't that every place?

57
00:02:31,578 --> 00:02:33,135
Hey, man. How you been?
I haven't seen you in...

58
00:02:33,271 --> 00:02:35,273
-Snake attack! (chuckles)
-(screaming)

59
00:02:35,408 --> 00:02:36,974
Oh. Mints.

60
00:02:37,109 --> 00:02:38,848
Sorry, folks.
I'm switching him to decaf.

61
00:02:38,983 --> 00:02:40,311
(chuckles)

62
00:02:40,446 --> 00:02:41,583
All right.

63
00:02:41,719 --> 00:02:43,344
-BOTH: Let's do this.
-(entry bell jingles)

64
00:02:43,479 --> 00:02:46,720
-(people gasping, screaming)
-(tires squealing)

65
00:02:49,053 --> 00:02:51,226
-(crashing)
-(car alarm whooping)

66
00:02:51,361 --> 00:02:54,221
-(tires squeal)
-(crashing)

67
00:02:56,527 --> 00:02:57,726
Guinea pig, huh?

68
00:02:57,861 --> 00:02:59,728
It's the Rolls-Royce of rodents.

69
00:02:59,864 --> 00:03:01,497
Yeah, but it's still a rodent.

70
00:03:01,632 --> 00:03:03,472
You know what I mean?

71
00:03:03,608 --> 00:03:05,634
-Don't mind us, just robbing
this place. -(gasping)

72
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:07,406
(screaming, frantic chatter)

73
00:03:07,541 --> 00:03:09,470
-(clattering)
-(screaming)

74
00:03:09,605 --> 00:03:10,944
(alarm ringing)

75
00:03:11,079 --> 00:03:13,513
♪ ♪

76
00:03:14,876 --> 00:03:17,352
(engine revs, tires squeal)

77
00:03:19,581 --> 00:03:20,780
Whoo! Yeah!

78
00:03:20,916 --> 00:03:22,614
-Go bad...
-Or go home.

79
00:03:22,749 --> 00:03:24,051
(both laugh)

80
00:03:28,261 --> 00:03:31,128
Hey, you. Get over here.

81
00:03:31,263 --> 00:03:33,725
Little bit closer.

82
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:36,162
Oh, I know what it is.

83
00:03:36,298 --> 00:03:39,971
You're afraid because
I'm the... the Big Bad Wolf.

84
00:03:40,107 --> 00:03:41,766
Well, I'm not surprised.

85
00:03:41,901 --> 00:03:43,669
I am the villain in every story.

86
00:03:43,804 --> 00:03:44,900
Isn't that right, Mr. Snake?

87
00:03:45,036 --> 00:03:46,307
(chuckling):
Yep.

88
00:03:46,443 --> 00:03:49,414
Say hello to Mr. Snake.

89
00:03:49,550 --> 00:03:51,350
<i>Serpentine,</i>
<i>safe-cracking machine.</i>

90
00:03:51,486 --> 00:03:53,575
<i>Imagine Houdini</i>
<i>but with no arms.</i>

91
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:55,712
<i>Kind of guy who'd tell you</i>
<i>the glass is half empty,</i>

92
00:03:55,848 --> 00:03:57,120
<i>then steal it from you.</i>

93
00:03:57,255 --> 00:03:58,620
He's also my best bud.

94
00:03:58,756 --> 00:04:01,083
(singsongy):
And today's his birthday!

95
00:04:01,218 --> 00:04:03,285
-Not relevant.
-He's a sweetheart.

96
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:05,095
-You're a sweetheart.
-(sirens wailing)

97
00:04:05,230 --> 00:04:07,298
Well, look who's here.

98
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:10,060
-Took 'em long enough.
-(engine revs)

99
00:04:14,038 --> 00:04:15,937
Watch this.

100
00:04:16,072 --> 00:04:17,665
Three.

101
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,706
Two. One.

102
00:04:21,245 --> 00:04:22,909
<i>And over here is Ms. Tarantula,</i>

103
00:04:23,045 --> 00:04:25,378
<i>our in-house hacker,</i>
<i>our pocket search engine,</i>

104
00:04:25,514 --> 00:04:26,983
<i>our traveling tech wizard.</i>

105
00:04:27,118 --> 00:04:28,814
<i>We call her Webs.</i>

106
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:32,887
(sirens whooping)

107
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:34,813
(horns honking)

108
00:04:34,948 --> 00:04:36,049
Very slick, Webs.

109
00:04:36,185 --> 00:04:37,424
I also took over
the police dispatch,

110
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,026
blurred their satellite
imaging system,

111
00:04:39,162 --> 00:04:40,427
grounded their chopper.

112
00:04:40,563 --> 00:04:42,193
(singsongy):
And one more thing.

113
00:04:42,328 --> 00:04:43,363
You didn't.

114
00:04:43,498 --> 00:04:45,066
I got a special delivery for...

115
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,363
Ah! Ooh! Don't eat me!

116
00:04:46,498 --> 00:04:48,467
Please! Don't eat me!

117
00:04:48,602 --> 00:04:51,136
Happy birthday,
Mr. Grumpy Pants.

118
00:04:51,272 --> 00:04:52,972
I think I hate you.

119
00:04:53,107 --> 00:04:55,109
(engine revving)

120
00:04:55,244 --> 00:04:57,170
(construction equipment beeping)

121
00:04:57,980 --> 00:04:59,446
(sirens wailing)

122
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,418
(officers groaning)

123
00:05:06,453 --> 00:05:08,154
(chuckling):
Guys, it's me.

124
00:05:08,290 --> 00:05:09,915
I was the construction worker.

125
00:05:10,051 --> 00:05:11,980
WOLF:
<i>And this is Mr. Shark,</i>

126
00:05:12,116 --> 00:05:13,623
<i>master of disguise,</i>

127
00:05:13,759 --> 00:05:16,661
<i>apex predator</i>
<i>of a thousand faces.</i>

128
00:05:17,831 --> 00:05:19,423
<i>His greatest trick:</i>
<i>stealing the</i> Mona Lisa

129
00:05:19,559 --> 00:05:22,395
<i>-disguised as the</i> Mona Lisa.
-(sirens wailing)

130
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:23,595
Dig that.

131
00:05:23,731 --> 00:05:25,035
Watch it, big tuna.

132
00:05:25,171 --> 00:05:26,267
I'm trying to work here.

133
00:05:26,403 --> 00:05:27,863
Keep it cool, baby.

134
00:05:27,999 --> 00:05:29,665
Birthdays should be chill.

135
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,837
(sirens wailing)

136
00:05:30,973 --> 00:05:32,569
WOLF:
<i>And rounding out the crew...</i>

137
00:05:32,704 --> 00:05:34,670
(thumping)

138
00:05:34,805 --> 00:05:35,980
Surprise!

139
00:05:36,115 --> 00:05:37,281
(Piranha laughing)

140
00:05:37,417 --> 00:05:38,915
WOLF:
<i>...is Mr. Piranha.</i>

141
00:05:39,751 --> 00:05:42,179
<i>He's a loose cannon</i>
<i>with a short fuse,</i>

142
00:05:42,314 --> 00:05:44,210
<i>willing to scrap</i>
<i>with anyone or anything.</i>

143
00:05:44,346 --> 00:05:46,014
<i>-He's brave.</i>
-(cackling)

144
00:05:46,149 --> 00:05:48,349
-(yelling)
<i>-He's fearless.</i>

145
00:05:48,484 --> 00:05:50,418
<i>Uh, who am I kidding?</i>
<i>He's crazy.</i>

146
00:05:50,553 --> 00:05:53,252
(laughs)<i> Santo cielo,</i>
that's a lot of po-po.

147
00:05:53,388 --> 00:05:56,956
Uh, Piranha,
did we forget something?

148
00:05:57,092 --> 00:05:58,761
-What?
-The present.

149
00:05:58,896 --> 00:06:00,532
-You know.
-Oh, um...

150
00:06:00,668 --> 00:06:02,836
Of-of course I didn't forget.

151
00:06:02,971 --> 00:06:05,296
-(toots) -You know you fart
when you lie, right?

152
00:06:05,432 --> 00:06:07,064
What? No, I fart
when I'm nervous.

153
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,510
Yeah. Nervous about lying.

154
00:06:08,645 --> 00:06:10,312
-(stomach burbling)
-(groans) I'm sorry.

155
00:06:10,447 --> 00:06:11,972
-(loud fart)
-OTHERS: Piranha!

156
00:06:12,107 --> 00:06:13,472
SHARK:
Don't breathe it in.

157
00:06:13,607 --> 00:06:14,845
-I breathed it in!
-(officers groaning, gasping)

158
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,574
WOLF:
<i>Yeah, they're a bit eccentric,</i>

159
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,416
<i>but when you're born us,</i>
<i>you don't exactly win</i>

160
00:06:18,552 --> 00:06:20,178
<i>many popularity contests.</i>

161
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:22,621
-(whimpers) Shark!
-OTHERS: Shark!

162
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:25,216
Do I wish people
didn't see us as monsters?

163
00:06:25,352 --> 00:06:26,716
Eight legs,
eight times the cardio.

164
00:06:26,852 --> 00:06:27,857
Monster!

165
00:06:27,992 --> 00:06:29,653
-WOLF:<i> Sure, I do.</i>
-What's up, papa?

166
00:06:29,789 --> 00:06:30,922
WOLF:<i> But these are</i>
<i>the cards we've been dealt,</i>

167
00:06:31,058 --> 00:06:32,490
so we might as well play 'em.

168
00:06:32,626 --> 00:06:33,898
Jackpot!

169
00:06:34,034 --> 00:06:35,392
Yes!

170
00:06:38,897 --> 00:06:40,830
♪ ♪

171
00:06:40,965 --> 00:06:42,773
(tires screech)

172
00:06:45,946 --> 00:06:47,203
Um...

173
00:06:47,338 --> 00:06:48,910
-What the thorax?
-Are you crazy?

174
00:06:49,045 --> 00:06:51,676
What? I just wanted
a longer car chase.

175
00:06:51,812 --> 00:06:53,343
It's the best part.

176
00:06:54,112 --> 00:06:56,020
(indistinct radio chatter)

177
00:06:56,156 --> 00:06:57,580
Chief! It's...

178
00:06:57,715 --> 00:06:59,185
Them.

179
00:06:59,321 --> 00:07:00,650
(grunts)

180
00:07:00,786 --> 00:07:02,122
Webs, hit it.

181
00:07:02,257 --> 00:07:05,094
("Stop, Drop, Roll" by
Can't Stop Won't Stop playing)

182
00:07:05,229 --> 00:07:06,789
Get them!

183
00:07:06,925 --> 00:07:10,292
(laughing, whooping)

184
00:07:14,028 --> 00:07:15,229
(clamoring)

185
00:07:15,365 --> 00:07:17,200
-(tires squealing)
-(sirens wailing)

186
00:07:19,511 --> 00:07:21,102
♪ Hooked on hip-hop phonics ♪

187
00:07:21,237 --> 00:07:22,635
♪ Yeah, it works for me ♪

188
00:07:22,771 --> 00:07:25,174
♪ So jump aboard,
yeah, this train is free ♪

189
00:07:25,309 --> 00:07:27,441
♪ The conductor,
let me toot my whistle ♪

190
00:07:27,577 --> 00:07:29,444
♪ The instructor
of the funky uncle fizzle ♪

191
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:32,152
♪ We be dancin' on a lake
when it ain't froze over ♪

192
00:07:32,287 --> 00:07:34,648
♪ We be walkin' on water while
you're sinkin' your rover ♪

193
00:07:34,784 --> 00:07:36,984
♪ If you step any closer,
you'll be eatin' some teeth ♪

194
00:07:37,119 --> 00:07:38,157
♪ So please step back... ♪

195
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:40,452
(laughing)

196
00:07:40,587 --> 00:07:42,395
I'm gonna put you guys away
for so long,

197
00:07:42,530 --> 00:07:44,962
your fleas will have fleas.

198
00:07:45,925 --> 00:07:46,968
(grunts)

199
00:07:47,103 --> 00:07:48,570
(all gasp)

200
00:07:49,965 --> 00:07:51,296
Chief. You want some cake?

201
00:07:51,432 --> 00:07:53,871
-You seem a little hangry.
-(laughter)

202
00:07:54,006 --> 00:07:55,474
Get that thing
out of my face before I...

203
00:07:55,609 --> 00:07:58,238
-Excuse me, Chief.
-What?

204
00:08:00,207 --> 00:08:01,747
-(screams)
-♪ Stop ♪

205
00:08:02,842 --> 00:08:04,314
♪ Drop ♪

206
00:08:04,450 --> 00:08:09,253
♪ Roll, roll ♪

207
00:08:09,388 --> 00:08:10,253
♪ Stop... ♪

208
00:08:10,388 --> 00:08:12,355
(sirens blaring)

209
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:13,851
(chuckles) You're mine.

210
00:08:13,986 --> 00:08:15,324
♪ Roll... ♪

211
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:17,387
(engine revs)

212
00:08:18,989 --> 00:08:20,830
<i>Hermano.</i>

213
00:08:22,158 --> 00:08:24,361
(tires squealing)

214
00:08:25,534 --> 00:08:27,003
(screaming)

215
00:08:27,139 --> 00:08:29,168
♪ I'm gonna get mine, mine,
stake mine, really ♪

216
00:08:29,304 --> 00:08:31,105
♪ Chi-Town cat
gettin' cheese like Philly ♪

217
00:08:31,241 --> 00:08:34,469
♪ Order steak at the grilly,
I flow chilly... ♪

218
00:08:35,279 --> 00:08:37,307
(all screaming)

219
00:08:38,183 --> 00:08:40,182
(all screaming)

220
00:08:40,317 --> 00:08:41,414
(birds chirping)

221
00:08:41,549 --> 00:08:43,184
(all screaming)

222
00:08:43,319 --> 00:08:46,315
♪ And you's a chicken nugget
head, dip it in my chitchat ♪

223
00:08:47,252 --> 00:08:48,883
-♪ Stop... ♪
-(buckles click)

224
00:08:49,019 --> 00:08:51,358
Yeah, we may be bad,

225
00:08:51,494 --> 00:08:53,161
but we're so good at it.

226
00:08:53,296 --> 00:08:55,595
(laughter)

227
00:08:55,731 --> 00:08:56,889
-(sirens wailing)
-(grunts)

228
00:08:57,024 --> 00:08:58,359
♪ Stop ♪

229
00:08:59,159 --> 00:09:00,292
♪ Drop... ♪

230
00:09:00,427 --> 00:09:02,467
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

231
00:09:02,603 --> 00:09:04,630
Keep running, Wolf!

232
00:09:04,765 --> 00:09:07,841
One of these days,
your luck is gonna run out!

233
00:09:08,969 --> 00:09:10,777
(song ends)

234
00:09:20,156 --> 00:09:22,381
♪ ♪

235
00:09:30,121 --> 00:09:32,094
(bell dings)

236
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:39,798
All right, Piranha, you're up.

237
00:09:39,933 --> 00:09:44,099
♪ Oh... ♪

238
00:09:44,234 --> 00:09:45,507
♪ Happy bir... ♪

239
00:09:45,642 --> 00:09:46,776
-(blows)
-(gasps)

240
00:09:46,912 --> 00:09:48,337
-Seriously?
-WOLF: Snake, come on.

241
00:09:48,473 --> 00:09:50,172
-At least make a toast.
-(Snake groans)

242
00:09:50,308 --> 00:09:51,639
-Toast! Come on!
-Come on.

243
00:09:51,774 --> 00:09:53,149
-SNAKE: Okay, okay. All right.
A toast. -Whoo!

244
00:09:53,284 --> 00:09:54,743
Fine.

245
00:09:54,879 --> 00:09:57,953
I've made a lot of enemies
in my time-- I mean, a lot--

246
00:09:58,088 --> 00:10:01,082
but out of all the people
in the world,

247
00:10:01,218 --> 00:10:02,725
I hate you guys the least.

248
00:10:02,861 --> 00:10:04,392
-Aw. -That was actually
kind of beautiful.

249
00:10:04,528 --> 00:10:05,928
You're a poet, man.

250
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:09,832
To Mr. Snake and his strange
dislike of birthdays.

251
00:10:09,967 --> 00:10:12,334
-TARANTULA: Yay!
-(others whooping, laughing)

252
00:10:12,470 --> 00:10:14,929
Everyone say, "Robbery."

253
00:10:15,064 --> 00:10:16,470
ALL:
Robbery.

254
00:10:16,606 --> 00:10:17,900
(chuckles):
Oh.

255
00:10:18,035 --> 00:10:19,870
Look at those dimples.

256
00:10:20,006 --> 00:10:21,741
-Happy birthday, buddy.
-Okay.

257
00:10:21,877 --> 00:10:23,679
-Now, dig in, fellas.
-Yes!

258
00:10:23,814 --> 00:10:25,748
-(laughs, munches wildly)
-Piranha!

259
00:10:25,883 --> 00:10:27,240
-WOLF: Don't do that.
-(Piranha slurping)

260
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:28,516
TARANTULA:
That was so gross.

261
00:10:28,651 --> 00:10:30,115
SHARK:
That was my lunch!

262
00:10:30,251 --> 00:10:32,116
-PIRANHA: You snooze, you lose.
-(Tarantula laughing)

263
00:10:32,251 --> 00:10:34,649
-WOLF: You like that.
-(Piranha chuckles)

264
00:10:34,784 --> 00:10:36,450
Nice.

265
00:10:37,284 --> 00:10:39,185
-Ooh, wow.
-(gasps)

266
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,784
I forgot we had those Push Pops.

267
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:43,526
Man, my tummy is rumbling
like a kraken right now.

268
00:10:43,662 --> 00:10:45,359
Yeah. Want it?

269
00:10:45,494 --> 00:10:47,533
You know he's not
gonna give it to you.

270
00:10:47,668 --> 00:10:49,526
No, I believe that deep down

271
00:10:49,661 --> 00:10:52,962
Snake is a kind
and generous soul.

272
00:10:53,098 --> 00:10:54,338
Why?

273
00:10:54,474 --> 00:10:56,299
Here. Take it.

274
00:10:56,435 --> 00:10:57,836
(laughing):
Oh, yeah!

275
00:10:57,971 --> 00:10:59,135
Pop me, please.

276
00:10:59,270 --> 00:11:01,038
-Ah...
-Ha!

277
00:11:01,173 --> 00:11:02,905
(chuckles) Sucker.

278
00:11:03,041 --> 00:11:06,342
Come on, man. Now you gonna
make me get all aggressive.

279
00:11:06,477 --> 00:11:08,342
-(clamoring)
-Animals.

280
00:11:08,478 --> 00:11:10,451
Spit it out! Spit it out!

281
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:11,922
Never!

282
00:11:12,057 --> 00:11:13,684
Let's see what they're saying
about us today.

283
00:11:13,819 --> 00:11:15,484
What up? It's Tiffany Fluffit,
Channel 6 Action News.

284
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:17,420
The Bad Guys
have struck again...

285
00:11:17,556 --> 00:11:20,522
Guys, guys, stop it.
We're on TV.

286
00:11:20,658 --> 00:11:22,095
-Ooh, ooh!
-...proving once more that they

287
00:11:22,231 --> 00:11:24,666
are the most diabolical
criminals of our time.

288
00:11:24,802 --> 00:11:27,628
Ooh, "diabolical." That's new.

289
00:11:27,763 --> 00:11:29,298
Know what it sounds like?
A cologne.

290
00:11:29,433 --> 00:11:30,665
(dramatically):
Diabolical.

291
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,568
TIFFANY: To address
this heinous crime spree

292
00:11:32,702 --> 00:11:35,678
is the newly elected governor,
Diane Foxington.

293
00:11:35,813 --> 00:11:37,077
-Governor?
-DIANE: Okay. Yeah.

294
00:11:37,212 --> 00:11:38,971
-I hear you. I hear you.
-(reporters clamoring)

295
00:11:39,107 --> 00:11:42,677
Listen, listen. We all know
how dastardly the Bad Guys are.

296
00:11:42,812 --> 00:11:45,754
-WOLF: You bet we are.
-But more than anything...

297
00:11:45,889 --> 00:11:48,354
(chuckles)
I feel sorry for them.

298
00:11:48,489 --> 00:11:50,116
What?

299
00:11:50,252 --> 00:11:51,858
These so-called Bad Guys

300
00:11:51,994 --> 00:11:54,628
are really just
second-rate has-beens.

301
00:11:54,764 --> 00:11:56,654
Behind their amateurish antics

302
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:58,930
and, frankly,
unoriginal capers--

303
00:11:59,064 --> 00:12:00,866
I mean, really, another bank?--

304
00:12:01,001 --> 00:12:03,295
is nothing but
a deep well of anger...

305
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:04,704
I ain't angry! You're angry!

306
00:12:04,839 --> 00:12:06,473
-...denial...
-Not true.

307
00:12:06,608 --> 00:12:07,741
...and self-loathing.

308
00:12:07,876 --> 00:12:09,877
The only one I self-loathe
is you.

309
00:12:10,012 --> 00:12:12,337
And those are holes
that no amount of cash

310
00:12:12,472 --> 00:12:15,574
or priceless art can ever fill.

311
00:12:17,575 --> 00:12:19,653
What's on the Food Network?

312
00:12:19,788 --> 00:12:21,312
DIANE:
So, can we just forget about...

313
00:12:21,447 --> 00:12:22,913
Who-who is she to judge us?

314
00:12:23,049 --> 00:12:24,888
-DIANE: ...and focus on more
positive things? -(growls)

315
00:12:25,023 --> 00:12:26,549
And what could be more positive

316
00:12:26,685 --> 00:12:28,687
than the Annual
Good Samaritan Awards,

317
00:12:28,823 --> 00:12:31,795
where tomorrow night I will
present the Golden Dolphin

318
00:12:31,930 --> 00:12:35,259
to this year's goodest citizen?

319
00:12:35,394 --> 00:12:36,632
I can't believe I voted for her.

320
00:12:36,767 --> 00:12:38,036
You voted for her?

321
00:12:38,171 --> 00:12:40,702
TARANTULA: What?
She's good on climate change.

322
00:12:40,837 --> 00:12:42,465
Wait. What's going on?

323
00:12:42,601 --> 00:12:45,107
You've got that twinkle
in your eye.

324
00:12:46,944 --> 00:12:50,105
Guys, who's up for another job?

325
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,513
A big one.

326
00:12:51,647 --> 00:12:53,114
(all gasp)

327
00:12:53,950 --> 00:12:55,749
SNAKE:
The Golden Dolphin.

328
00:12:55,885 --> 00:12:57,378
-Seriously?
-Oh.

329
00:12:57,514 --> 00:12:59,022
I thought I was the crazy one.

330
00:12:59,158 --> 00:13:01,517
That job has broken
every criminal who's tried it.

331
00:13:01,652 --> 00:13:04,187
<i>The Bucharest Bandits,</i>
<i>Lucky Jim.</i>

332
00:13:04,323 --> 00:13:05,995
SHARK:
<i>The Crimson Paw.</i>

333
00:13:06,130 --> 00:13:07,829
Actually, the Crimson Paw
was never arrested.

334
00:13:07,965 --> 00:13:10,290
Yeah, but he never stole
anything again.

335
00:13:10,425 --> 00:13:12,034
Snake, what better way

336
00:13:12,169 --> 00:13:14,537
to wipe that smirk
off the governor's fuzzy face

337
00:13:14,672 --> 00:13:15,967
than stealing the Golden Dolphin

338
00:13:16,103 --> 00:13:17,970
from right under her whiskers?

339
00:13:18,106 --> 00:13:20,700
This is the Holy Grail
of thievery.

340
00:13:20,835 --> 00:13:22,910
If we pull this off,
we'll cement our legacy

341
00:13:23,046 --> 00:13:25,303
as the greatest criminals
of all time.

342
00:13:25,438 --> 00:13:26,939
Whoa, whoa, buddy.

343
00:13:27,075 --> 00:13:29,576
I thought we weren't supposed
to make things personal.

344
00:13:29,712 --> 00:13:31,612
Besides, we've got
a good thing going here.

345
00:13:31,747 --> 00:13:35,682
Friends, freedom,
and just look at this loot.

346
00:13:36,485 --> 00:13:37,790
All right, you're right.
Forget it.

347
00:13:37,925 --> 00:13:40,092
-The Dolphin job is off.
-Good.

348
00:13:40,227 --> 00:13:42,529
I guess the pig
will get his trophy after all.

349
00:13:42,665 --> 00:13:44,826
Yeah, I guess he would...

350
00:13:44,962 --> 00:13:46,566
What do you mean, "pig"?

351
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:48,166
Oh, yes, did I not mention that?

352
00:13:48,302 --> 00:13:50,761
That's weird. I thought
I mentioned that it was, uh...

353
00:13:51,936 --> 00:13:53,295
The Good Samaritan is...

354
00:13:53,431 --> 00:13:54,604
A guinea pig?

355
00:13:54,739 --> 00:13:56,266
(slurping)

356
00:13:56,402 --> 00:13:57,673
What do you say, Snakey?

357
00:13:57,808 --> 00:13:59,041
Better than cake.

358
00:13:59,176 --> 00:14:00,643
-(laughter)
-TARANTULA: Right.

359
00:14:00,779 --> 00:14:03,439
(groans) Okay. Fine.

360
00:14:03,574 --> 00:14:05,146
But he better be delicious.

361
00:14:05,282 --> 00:14:07,352
(laughs)
Are we all in this together?

362
00:14:07,487 --> 00:14:09,345
♪ ♪

363
00:14:09,481 --> 00:14:11,044
<i>So here's the plan.</i>

364
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:13,416
<i>Like every year,</i>
<i>the ceremony will be held</i>

365
00:14:13,551 --> 00:14:15,224
<i>at the Museum of Fine Arts,</i>

366
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,785
<i>where the Golden Dolphin</i>
<i>will be positioned</i>

367
00:14:17,921 --> 00:14:20,397
<i>just beyond</i>
<i>the backstage curtain.</i>

368
00:14:20,532 --> 00:14:21,724
Sounds easy.

369
00:14:21,859 --> 00:14:23,891
Sounds easy,<i> hermano,</i>
but to get there,

370
00:14:24,026 --> 00:14:26,264
we'll need to bypass
three levels of security.

371
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,829
So, step one:
We'll need to blend in.

372
00:14:28,965 --> 00:14:30,597
("Howlin' for You"
by The Black Keys playing)

373
00:14:30,733 --> 00:14:33,207
♪ Baby, I'm howlin' for you ♪

374
00:14:35,212 --> 00:14:37,142
♪ Da-da da-da da,
da-da da-da da... ♪

375
00:14:37,277 --> 00:14:38,904
WOLF:
<i>Professor Marmalade,</i>

376
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:41,182
<i>this year's recipient</i>
<i>of the Golden Dolphin,</i>

377
00:14:41,317 --> 00:14:43,712
<i>the most annoying good creature</i>
<i>on the planet.</i>

378
00:14:43,847 --> 00:14:46,317
Professor, in the past year,
you've stopped wars,

379
00:14:46,453 --> 00:14:48,857
fed the hungry
and saved countless pandas.

380
00:14:48,993 --> 00:14:50,581
Some have described
your goodness

381
00:14:50,716 --> 00:14:52,651
as second only to Mother Teresa.

382
00:14:52,787 --> 00:14:55,227
Oh, Tiffany,
it's not a competition.

383
00:14:55,362 --> 00:14:57,792
And if it were, it would
really be more of a tie.

384
00:14:57,928 --> 00:15:01,001
But we can all agree that
there is a flower of goodness

385
00:15:01,137 --> 00:15:04,061
inside all of us,
just waiting to blossom.

386
00:15:04,197 --> 00:15:07,003
WOLF:<i> Once inside,</i>
<i>there are two armored doors.</i>

387
00:15:07,138 --> 00:15:09,339
<i>The first can only be opened by</i>

388
00:15:09,474 --> 00:15:11,111
<i>a special key card</i>
<i>that is carried</i>

389
00:15:11,246 --> 00:15:13,003
<i>by our dear friend,</i>
<i>the chief of police.</i>

390
00:15:13,139 --> 00:15:15,004
<i>The second is outfitted</i>
<i>with a retinal scanner</i>

391
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:17,810
<i>and guarded by</i>
<i>an elite special ops unit</i>

392
00:15:17,946 --> 00:15:20,445
<i>trained to strike first</i>
<i>and ask questions later.</i>

393
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:22,087
-(fly buzzes)
-(whooshing)

394
00:15:22,222 --> 00:15:24,420
<i>Governor Foxington</i>
<i>is the only one</i>

395
00:15:24,556 --> 00:15:26,388
<i>who has clearance</i>
<i>to open the second door.</i>

396
00:15:26,524 --> 00:15:28,792
<i>So, step two:</i>
<i>She and I will need to get</i>

397
00:15:28,927 --> 00:15:30,587
<i>up close and personal.</i>

398
00:15:30,723 --> 00:15:32,387
Enjoy your evening,
Mr. Ambassador.

399
00:15:32,522 --> 00:15:33,564
Thank you, ma'am.

400
00:15:33,699 --> 00:15:35,097
Interesting piece.

401
00:15:35,233 --> 00:15:38,626
Trashy, pointless
and pretentious.

402
00:15:38,762 --> 00:15:41,137
Hmm. They say that art reveals

403
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:42,937
more about the viewer
than the artist.

404
00:15:43,073 --> 00:15:44,499
-(chuckles)
-Mister...

405
00:15:44,634 --> 00:15:46,676
Poodleton. Oliver Poodleton.

406
00:15:46,811 --> 00:15:47,777
DIANE:
Uh... okay.

407
00:15:47,912 --> 00:15:49,812
It's about time someone stood up

408
00:15:49,948 --> 00:15:52,181
to those diabolical Bad Guys.

409
00:15:52,317 --> 00:15:55,315
Though, I've got to say,
no one's succeeded yet.

410
00:15:55,451 --> 00:15:58,043
Eh. I don't think
it'll be that hard.

411
00:15:58,179 --> 00:16:00,186
I have a feeling it'll be
harder than you think.

412
00:16:00,321 --> 00:16:02,318
I'd say they're
one epic job away

413
00:16:02,453 --> 00:16:04,157
from cementing their legacy.

414
00:16:04,293 --> 00:16:06,753
-(Diane laughing)
-(Wolf chuckles)

415
00:16:06,889 --> 00:16:08,628
Mr. Poodleton,
you're-you're funny.

416
00:16:08,763 --> 00:16:10,198
I am?

417
00:16:10,333 --> 00:16:12,591
The only legacy they're
cementing is life in prison.

418
00:16:12,726 --> 00:16:14,427
Did you see their last job?

419
00:16:14,562 --> 00:16:16,037
Ugh. Unsecured exits,

420
00:16:16,172 --> 00:16:18,431
crude disguises,
compulsive showboating.

421
00:16:18,566 --> 00:16:19,932
I mean, it was a mess.

422
00:16:20,068 --> 00:16:22,735
All the classic signs
of a crew in decline.

423
00:16:22,871 --> 00:16:25,803
Next, they're gonna
make it personal.

424
00:16:25,939 --> 00:16:28,448
That's when you know
they're toast.

425
00:16:29,317 --> 00:16:31,719
(chuckles):
Uh, well, that's your opinion.

426
00:16:31,854 --> 00:16:34,378
It is, and I'm the governor.

427
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:39,484
As for the sculpture,
I think it's about perspective.

428
00:16:39,619 --> 00:16:41,326
If you look closely enough,

429
00:16:41,461 --> 00:16:45,995
even trash can be recycled
into something beautiful.

430
00:16:46,131 --> 00:16:48,157
WOLF:
How about that?

431
00:16:48,292 --> 00:16:52,636
I guess some things
aren't always as they appear.

432
00:16:52,771 --> 00:16:53,970
That reminds me.

433
00:16:54,106 --> 00:16:55,767
May I? I can't miss a photo op

434
00:16:55,902 --> 00:16:57,407
with the governor
and a pile of garbage.

435
00:16:57,542 --> 00:17:00,976
Oh, Mr. Poodleton,
you're too hard on yourself.

436
00:17:01,112 --> 00:17:02,636
-Hey...
-(camera clicks)

437
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:05,145
(quiet chatter, laughter)

438
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:06,748
WOLF:
Okay, friends.

439
00:17:06,884 --> 00:17:08,684
It's showtime.

440
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:10,285
♪ ♪

441
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:12,487
<i>Once we're in,</i>
<i>it's on to step three:</i>

442
00:17:12,622 --> 00:17:15,191
<i>We split up</i>
<i>and we take our positions.</i>

443
00:17:15,327 --> 00:17:18,885
Officers, if the Bad Guys
crash this event,

444
00:17:19,021 --> 00:17:20,989
I am definitely
going to lose my job,

445
00:17:21,124 --> 00:17:24,330
and I will not hesitate
to take you down with me.

446
00:17:24,466 --> 00:17:26,202
-Now, move out.
-OFFICERS: Yes, ma'am!

447
00:17:26,337 --> 00:17:27,862
Hut, hut, hut, hut,
hut, hut, hut, hut,

448
00:17:27,997 --> 00:17:29,703
hut, hut, hut, hut, hut,
hut, hut, hut, hut...

449
00:17:29,838 --> 00:17:32,064
♪ ♪

450
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:46,578
Mic's on.
Everyone on comms, do you copy?

451
00:17:46,714 --> 00:17:47,812
-Copy.
-Copy. -Copy.

452
00:17:47,948 --> 00:17:49,524
(high-pitched voice):
Copy.

453
00:17:49,659 --> 00:17:52,523
♪ ♪

454
00:17:57,731 --> 00:17:59,859
(laughs)

455
00:18:08,173 --> 00:18:09,902
A drink for the pretty lady?

456
00:18:10,037 --> 00:18:12,677
No, thank you. My life is
too complicated right now.

457
00:18:12,812 --> 00:18:14,510
Uh, uh...

458
00:18:21,711 --> 00:18:24,288
(whistling a tune)

459
00:18:29,289 --> 00:18:31,889
♪ ♪

460
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:43,630
Boys, it's Dolphin season.

461
00:18:43,765 --> 00:18:44,905
(muffled grunting)

462
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,602
(pants zip)

463
00:18:46,736 --> 00:18:49,245
Copy that. I'm on the move.

464
00:18:50,382 --> 00:18:52,215
Unit two, is the backstage
area still secure?

465
00:18:52,350 --> 00:18:53,579
OFFICER (over radio):
Unit two. All clear.

466
00:18:53,714 --> 00:18:56,019
This is where
all the training pays off.

467
00:18:56,154 --> 00:18:57,746
-(grunts, groans)
-Oh, pardon me.

468
00:18:57,882 --> 00:18:59,712
-Terribly sorry.
-Not a problem, sir.

469
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,752
Keep your eyes open, boys.

470
00:19:01,888 --> 00:19:05,854
They could be anywhere,
just waiting to humiliate us.

471
00:19:06,663 --> 00:19:08,389
(laughs)

472
00:19:08,525 --> 00:19:10,091
Wolf is in position.

473
00:19:10,227 --> 00:19:12,566
(over radio): Piranha, you all
penguin-suited and booted?

474
00:19:12,702 --> 00:19:16,133
Affirmative. I'm a clean, mean,
Dolphin-stealing machine.

475
00:19:16,268 --> 00:19:18,162
What's going on, guys?

476
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:22,936
(indistinct chatter)

477
00:19:28,981 --> 00:19:31,218
♪ ♪

478
00:19:32,654 --> 00:19:34,353
(grunts)

479
00:19:41,454 --> 00:19:43,625
(woman grunting)

480
00:19:54,433 --> 00:19:56,164
(both yelp)

481
00:19:58,107 --> 00:19:59,807
(woman gasping)

482
00:19:59,943 --> 00:20:01,309
(sighs)

483
00:20:01,444 --> 00:20:03,539
-Here, let me help you.
-Ooh.

484
00:20:03,675 --> 00:20:04,907
Are you okay, ma'am?

485
00:20:05,043 --> 00:20:08,076
(panting):
Oh, my gracious, yes.

486
00:20:08,212 --> 00:20:11,747
I may be dizzy, but I'm alive,
thanks to you.

487
00:20:11,882 --> 00:20:13,446
-WOLF: What are you...
-Oh.

488
00:20:13,582 --> 00:20:14,823
Mm.

489
00:20:14,958 --> 00:20:16,385
(Wolf whimpers)

490
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:19,119
Thank you, dear.

491
00:20:19,931 --> 00:20:22,963
You're such a good boy.

492
00:20:23,098 --> 00:20:25,063
(chuckles softly)

493
00:20:25,198 --> 00:20:26,999
(woman grunting)

494
00:20:27,134 --> 00:20:29,371
♪ ♪

495
00:20:31,874 --> 00:20:34,100
(whimpers)

496
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:43,382
All good, brother?

497
00:20:43,518 --> 00:20:46,787
Yeah, all... a-all good.
Yeah, yeah.

498
00:20:46,922 --> 00:20:48,345
Um... (splutters)

499
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:50,958
Webs, what do you say about
moving on to step four?

500
00:20:51,093 --> 00:20:53,723
Copy that. Shark, you're up.

501
00:20:53,858 --> 00:20:56,028
-Do your thing.
-(gasps) Do I get to improvise?

502
00:20:56,163 --> 00:20:58,063
Yes, fine. Improvise.

503
00:20:58,197 --> 00:20:59,829
But please be subtle.

504
00:20:59,965 --> 00:21:01,697
Mm-hmm.

505
00:21:03,229 --> 00:21:05,464
(high-pitched voice):
I'm having a baby!

506
00:21:05,599 --> 00:21:06,931
Is there a doctor?

507
00:21:07,066 --> 00:21:09,001
Or perhaps
several security guards

508
00:21:09,136 --> 00:21:10,935
that could leave their post
and help me?

509
00:21:11,071 --> 00:21:12,207
-(both gasp)
-(guests murmuring)

510
00:21:12,342 --> 00:21:14,038
(elevator bell dings)

511
00:21:16,917 --> 00:21:19,076
(lock beeping)

512
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:25,048
♪ ♪

513
00:21:31,061 --> 00:21:32,660
"Fish surprise"?

514
00:21:33,658 --> 00:21:35,525
Surprise! (yells)

515
00:21:35,660 --> 00:21:37,664
(guards grunting)

516
00:21:42,703 --> 00:21:44,364
Hey, Webs,
can you enhance this...

517
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:47,069
TARANTULA: Done. Eight steps
ahead of you, Wolfie.

518
00:21:53,410 --> 00:21:54,348
(laughs)

519
00:21:54,484 --> 00:21:55,714
ANNOUNCER:
Ladies and gentlemen,

520
00:21:55,849 --> 00:21:58,777
your emcee for
the Good Samaritan Awards...

521
00:21:58,913 --> 00:22:00,247
(breathing heavily)

522
00:22:00,382 --> 00:22:02,216
WOLF (over radio):
All right, Shark, we're in.

523
00:22:02,352 --> 00:22:04,425
(normal voice): Oops,
I forgot, I'm not pregnant.

524
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,587
ANNOUNCER:
...president of the committee,

525
00:22:06,723 --> 00:22:09,023
Governor Diane Foxington.

526
00:22:09,158 --> 00:22:11,766
Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you so much.

527
00:22:11,901 --> 00:22:14,060
Thank you.

528
00:22:14,195 --> 00:22:17,096
Last year,
we faced our biggest test

529
00:22:17,231 --> 00:22:20,705
when a meteorite crashed
into our dear city.

530
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:23,802
That meteorite didn't just make
a hole in our city.

531
00:22:23,938 --> 00:22:25,806
It made a hole in our hearts.

532
00:22:25,941 --> 00:22:27,744
-CROWD: Aw.
-(Shark sniffles)

533
00:22:27,879 --> 00:22:30,148
But even in tragedy,
Professor Marmalade,

534
00:22:30,283 --> 00:22:31,976
he did what he does so well.

535
00:22:32,112 --> 00:22:34,482
He made us look
at things differently.

536
00:22:34,618 --> 00:22:36,314
And thanks to you, Marmalade,

537
00:22:36,450 --> 00:22:40,053
the Love Crater Meteorite
will forever serve as a symbol

538
00:22:40,188 --> 00:22:43,828
of how there is good
even in the worst places.

539
00:22:43,963 --> 00:22:45,422
(applause)

540
00:22:45,557 --> 00:22:46,823
Whoo!

541
00:22:46,959 --> 00:22:48,691
(Diane continues indistinctly)

542
00:22:48,827 --> 00:22:50,259
(Piranha laughs, grunts)

543
00:22:53,137 --> 00:22:55,440
(all grunt)

544
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:58,299
(groans) Hurry up.

545
00:22:59,108 --> 00:23:00,367
(grunts)

546
00:23:00,502 --> 00:23:02,112
...and successfully reversed
climate change

547
00:23:02,247 --> 00:23:04,513
for the well-being of all of us.

548
00:23:04,648 --> 00:23:08,243
This is going
surprisingly smoothly.

549
00:23:09,645 --> 00:23:10,849
(gasps)

550
00:23:13,122 --> 00:23:15,183
(Wolf yelps)

551
00:23:16,017 --> 00:23:18,219
What the molt is that?

552
00:23:18,355 --> 00:23:19,759
WOLF: The Wolf Piranha
Snake Shark Tarantula

553
00:23:19,894 --> 00:23:21,761
-Protection System.
-TARANTULA: The WPSST?

554
00:23:21,896 --> 00:23:24,264
-This was not supposed
to happen. -What?

555
00:23:24,399 --> 00:23:26,293
Guys, calm down. I'm on it.

556
00:23:26,428 --> 00:23:29,794
Initiating WPSST override
protocol. (chuckles)

557
00:23:29,930 --> 00:23:31,104
Get it, queen!

558
00:23:31,239 --> 00:23:32,607
(computer buzzes)

559
00:23:32,742 --> 00:23:34,873
-WOLF: Did it work?
-Just give me five minutes.

560
00:23:35,008 --> 00:23:38,343
And now, please join me
in welcoming to the stage...

561
00:23:38,478 --> 00:23:40,112
We don't have five minutes.

562
00:23:40,248 --> 00:23:42,342
...Professor Marmalade.

563
00:23:42,478 --> 00:23:43,416
Aw.

564
00:23:43,552 --> 00:23:45,777
We love you,
Professor Marmalade!

565
00:23:45,913 --> 00:23:47,112
The pig is on the move.

566
00:23:47,247 --> 00:23:49,380
I repeat, the pig
is on the move.

567
00:23:49,515 --> 00:23:51,881
Webs, Webs, the curtain's
going up any minute.

568
00:23:52,017 --> 00:23:53,082
It's not letting me in.

569
00:23:53,218 --> 00:23:54,384
Check your system preferences.

570
00:23:54,519 --> 00:23:55,818
You probably need
to download a driver.

571
00:23:55,954 --> 00:23:56,920
Try rebooting.

572
00:23:57,056 --> 00:23:58,429
Oh, my gosh, you fixed it.

573
00:23:58,564 --> 00:23:59,663
-SNAKE and WOLF: Really?
-No!

574
00:23:59,798 --> 00:24:01,561
-(door rattling)
-CHIEF: Hey, Larry.

575
00:24:01,696 --> 00:24:02,664
Come on, open up.

576
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:04,460
What did we say
about locking doors?

577
00:24:04,596 --> 00:24:06,931
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.
Shark, I got a situation here.

578
00:24:07,067 --> 00:24:08,263
SHARK:
Copy that. I'm on my way.

579
00:24:08,398 --> 00:24:10,172
-(stomach burbling)
-(grunts)

580
00:24:10,307 --> 00:24:11,542
Hurry up, guys.

581
00:24:11,677 --> 00:24:14,172
Time to turn this baby
on beast mode.

582
00:24:16,346 --> 00:24:18,615
Eat it, WPSST!

583
00:24:22,981 --> 00:24:24,621
Please, not now. (whimpers)

584
00:24:24,756 --> 00:24:26,414
-Wolf. -Wait, wait, wait.
No, no, Piranha!

585
00:24:26,549 --> 00:24:29,284
-This award is for...
-(Piranha farts loudly)

586
00:24:30,319 --> 00:24:32,090
(clears throat)
As I was saying...

587
00:24:32,225 --> 00:24:35,598
(gasps) No, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no!

588
00:24:38,069 --> 00:24:39,669
(sniffing)

589
00:24:39,804 --> 00:24:42,470
-Piranha! Are you kidding me?
-PIRANHA: Sorry!

590
00:24:42,606 --> 00:24:44,696
And that's why
my Gala for Goodness

591
00:24:44,832 --> 00:24:47,608
will raise all the money needed
for those less fortunate.

592
00:24:47,743 --> 00:24:48,977
-CHIEF: Come on!
-(pounding at door)

593
00:24:49,112 --> 00:24:50,275
(inhales deeply)

594
00:24:50,878 --> 00:24:53,307
I'm starting
to get mad here, Larry.

595
00:24:54,410 --> 00:24:55,848
-WOLF: Webs! Webs!
-(muffled grunting)

596
00:24:55,983 --> 00:24:59,620
And now the moment
we've all been waiting for.

597
00:25:01,016 --> 00:25:03,723
-(whimpering)
-Whoa!

598
00:25:09,261 --> 00:25:10,696
(groans)

599
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:15,124
SHARK (high-pitched voice):
Excuse me.

600
00:25:15,260 --> 00:25:16,766
Is this the ladies' room?

601
00:25:16,901 --> 00:25:18,931
Oh, uh, y-you need
to take a right

602
00:25:19,067 --> 00:25:20,941
at the end of the hall, ma'am.

603
00:25:21,075 --> 00:25:23,367
(gasping)

604
00:25:26,212 --> 00:25:28,504
Yes. Whoop-bam!

605
00:25:29,809 --> 00:25:30,874
Oh, come on!

606
00:25:31,677 --> 00:25:35,284
And now it is my honor
to award Professor Marmalade

607
00:25:35,420 --> 00:25:39,481
with the Golden Dolphin!

608
00:25:41,185 --> 00:25:42,490
-(gasps) No.
-No.

609
00:25:42,626 --> 00:25:43,758
(normal voice):
Yes!

610
00:25:43,894 --> 00:25:46,128
(high-pitched voice):
I mean, yes!

611
00:25:46,263 --> 00:25:47,928
What?

612
00:25:50,168 --> 00:25:52,033
(screams)

613
00:25:52,969 --> 00:25:55,269
Everyone, everyone, uh,
please don't panic.

614
00:25:55,404 --> 00:25:56,706
Just stay calm.

615
00:25:56,841 --> 00:25:59,142
I'm-I'm sure there's
an explanation for this.

616
00:25:59,278 --> 00:26:00,400
(gasping, murmuring)

617
00:26:00,535 --> 00:26:04,009
I repeat, uh,
please do not panic.

618
00:26:05,613 --> 00:26:07,279
Nice work, everybody.

619
00:26:07,414 --> 00:26:10,415
Now, let's make like a wolf
and get the pack out of here.

620
00:26:10,551 --> 00:26:12,417
Ah, wordplay.

621
00:26:12,552 --> 00:26:13,720
I don't get it.

622
00:26:13,855 --> 00:26:15,713
MARMALADE:
Diane, Diane, if I may...

623
00:26:15,849 --> 00:26:17,924
-(microphone feedback squeals)
-You have to understand,

624
00:26:18,060 --> 00:26:21,192
I didn't bring hope back
to the city for an award.

625
00:26:21,328 --> 00:26:25,233
I did these good things because
of how they made me feel.

626
00:26:25,369 --> 00:26:26,859
That tingly feeling I get.

627
00:26:26,995 --> 00:26:28,300
That shiver up my spine.

628
00:26:28,436 --> 00:26:32,205
The wag in my tiny tail.

629
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:34,165
Because, you see,

630
00:26:34,301 --> 00:26:38,546
being good just feels so good.

631
00:26:38,681 --> 00:26:42,682
And when you're good,
you're loved.

632
00:26:43,881 --> 00:26:45,781
-(gasps, whimpers)
-Wolf?

633
00:26:45,916 --> 00:26:47,311
-Wolf?
-What are you doing?

634
00:26:47,446 --> 00:26:49,414
SNAKE, SHARK and PIRANHA:
Go!

635
00:26:49,549 --> 00:26:51,354
-It's the Bad Guys!
-(guests screaming)

636
00:26:51,489 --> 00:26:52,659
Arrest them!

637
00:26:52,794 --> 00:26:53,554
OFFICERS:
Hut, hut, hut, hut, hut, hut,

638
00:26:53,690 --> 00:26:54,924
hut, hut, hut, hut, hut,

639
00:26:55,059 --> 00:26:56,886
hut, hut, hut, hut, hut,
hut, hut, hut, hut.

640
00:26:57,021 --> 00:26:58,121
(officers growl)

641
00:26:58,257 --> 00:26:59,562
They stole the Golden Dolphin!

642
00:26:59,698 --> 00:27:02,525
Come on, you can't prove that.

643
00:27:04,462 --> 00:27:06,330
(high-pitched voice):
My baby!

644
00:27:06,466 --> 00:27:07,996
-On your knees, Bad Guys.
-(knuckles crack)

645
00:27:08,132 --> 00:27:09,229
With your hands up.

646
00:27:09,365 --> 00:27:11,405
Never! We're out of here.

647
00:27:11,540 --> 00:27:14,002
♪ ♪

648
00:27:14,137 --> 00:27:16,373
So long, suckers.

649
00:27:22,512 --> 00:27:25,220
Well, this just got
a little weird.

650
00:27:25,355 --> 00:27:27,216
(siren whooping)

651
00:27:27,351 --> 00:27:29,023
TIFFANY:
The Bad Guys go bust.

652
00:27:29,158 --> 00:27:32,156
The nefarious fivesome
has finally been captured.

653
00:27:32,292 --> 00:27:34,929
And I, Tiffany Fluffit,
am first on the scene.

654
00:27:35,064 --> 00:27:37,733
Wow. You know, I-I just
realized that I have devoted

655
00:27:37,868 --> 00:27:40,334
my entire adult life
to putting you in jail.

656
00:27:40,470 --> 00:27:42,062
You are my purpose.

657
00:27:42,197 --> 00:27:43,965
Without you, who am I?

658
00:27:44,100 --> 00:27:45,398
Ah, I'm just kidding.

659
00:27:45,534 --> 00:27:47,198
This is the best moment
of my life!

660
00:27:47,334 --> 00:27:48,376
-(smack)
-(Wolf whimpers)

661
00:27:48,512 --> 00:27:51,176
It's the end of the Bad Guys.

662
00:27:51,312 --> 00:27:52,614
No!

663
00:27:52,749 --> 00:27:54,639
Get your hands off of me!
(screams)

664
00:27:54,774 --> 00:27:57,150
Ooh, you're begging
for a biting right now.

665
00:27:57,285 --> 00:27:58,687
Wolf!

666
00:28:01,989 --> 00:28:03,723
TIFFANY: Professor Marmalade!
Madam Governor!

667
00:28:03,859 --> 00:28:05,583
Ooh, Professor Marmalade!
Madam Governor!

668
00:28:05,718 --> 00:28:07,827
-Madam Governor!
-One at a time. One at a time.

669
00:28:10,390 --> 00:28:11,631
-Hey. Hey!
-Excuse me.

670
00:28:11,767 --> 00:28:13,591
-(people gasp)
-Sorry to interrupt.

671
00:28:13,726 --> 00:28:16,428
I just wanted to congratulate
the governor here.

672
00:28:16,563 --> 00:28:19,036
I got to say,
you really got us pegged.

673
00:28:19,171 --> 00:28:23,399
We're just a deep well
of anger and self-loathing.

674
00:28:23,534 --> 00:28:25,367
-Denial.
-Sure. That, too.

675
00:28:25,502 --> 00:28:26,574
-Narcissism.
-Yeah. Yeah.

676
00:28:26,710 --> 00:28:27,876
Emotional emptiness.

677
00:28:28,012 --> 00:28:29,412
-So we're on the same page.
-Hmm.

678
00:28:29,547 --> 00:28:31,506
What is he doing?

679
00:28:31,642 --> 00:28:34,677
Sadly, we were never
given a chance

680
00:28:34,812 --> 00:28:38,283
to be anything more
than second-rate criminals.

681
00:28:38,417 --> 00:28:40,890
If only there was someone
who could help

682
00:28:41,025 --> 00:28:44,551
the flower of goodness
inside us blossom.

683
00:28:44,687 --> 00:28:46,960
Some icon of love
and forgiveness,

684
00:28:47,095 --> 00:28:50,393
like, uh, I don't know,
Mother Teresa.

685
00:28:50,529 --> 00:28:53,460
Best thing is to just
throw us in jail

686
00:28:53,596 --> 00:28:56,097
for the rest
of our hopeless lives.

687
00:28:56,232 --> 00:28:57,905
Yeah, that's the plan.

688
00:28:58,041 --> 00:28:59,672
-Wait, wait, wait, no, no.
-(grunting)

689
00:28:59,808 --> 00:29:01,377
-Get in there.
-Ow!

690
00:29:01,513 --> 00:29:03,439
MARMALADE:
Wait.

691
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:05,481
Uh, beg... beg pardon?

692
00:29:05,616 --> 00:29:07,514
Mr. Wolf may be a savage beast.

693
00:29:07,650 --> 00:29:09,175
Basically walking garbage.

694
00:29:09,311 --> 00:29:10,650
Sorry, I'm making a point.

695
00:29:10,785 --> 00:29:12,379
Do what you need to do, pal.

696
00:29:12,514 --> 00:29:14,546
But how can we say
they're hopeless

697
00:29:14,682 --> 00:29:16,882
if they've never
been given a chance?

698
00:29:17,018 --> 00:29:19,990
What if... what if we tried
a little experiment, Diane?

699
00:29:20,126 --> 00:29:22,623
As you know,
my Gala for Goodness,

700
00:29:22,759 --> 00:29:26,458
the "hashtag charity event
of the year," is coming up.

701
00:29:26,594 --> 00:29:28,327
If I can prove
to everyone at that gala

702
00:29:28,462 --> 00:29:29,860
that the Bad Guys have changed,

703
00:29:29,996 --> 00:29:32,504
will you set them free
and give them a clean start?

704
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:33,938
(crowd gasping, murmuring)

705
00:29:34,074 --> 00:29:36,140
-What? Professor Marmalade!
-WOLF: Ow!

706
00:29:36,276 --> 00:29:38,509
No, no, no, no, no.
Don't you see what he's doing?

707
00:29:38,644 --> 00:29:40,137
He's playing you.

708
00:29:40,273 --> 00:29:41,346
But it was my idea.

709
00:29:41,481 --> 00:29:42,606
It was his idea.

710
00:29:42,742 --> 00:29:44,608
But only because
you made him have it.

711
00:29:44,743 --> 00:29:46,952
Madam Governor,
you can't just let them go.

712
00:29:47,087 --> 00:29:49,345
Professor, I'm not about to put
the safety of the city

713
00:29:49,481 --> 00:29:51,423
on the line for an experiment.

714
00:29:51,559 --> 00:29:53,056
Excuse me, Madam Governor.

715
00:29:53,192 --> 00:29:56,787
I seem to remember that
a wise person once said,

716
00:29:56,923 --> 00:30:01,129
"Even trash can be recycled
into something beautiful."

717
00:30:02,127 --> 00:30:03,868
(chuckles softly)

718
00:30:04,766 --> 00:30:06,067
Okay. I'm game.

719
00:30:06,202 --> 00:30:08,732
But only because it's you,
Professor.

720
00:30:08,868 --> 00:30:09,973
No!

721
00:30:10,108 --> 00:30:12,171
We'll hold on to the Dolphin
until the gala.

722
00:30:12,307 --> 00:30:15,577
Just to remove
any unnecessary temptation.

723
00:30:15,713 --> 00:30:17,745
Of course. Good thinking.

724
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:19,813
That's why you're governor.

725
00:30:19,948 --> 00:30:22,219
Now that everyone's happy...

726
00:30:22,354 --> 00:30:23,675
Not happy.

727
00:30:23,811 --> 00:30:26,313
...I, Rupert Marmalade
the Fourth,

728
00:30:26,449 --> 00:30:28,383
will turn the Bad Guys into...

729
00:30:28,519 --> 00:30:30,259
-the Good Guys!
-(cameras clicking)

730
00:30:30,394 --> 00:30:32,862
(people gasping)

731
00:30:34,863 --> 00:30:37,131
I think these belong to you.

732
00:30:37,267 --> 00:30:38,658
Hey.

733
00:30:39,760 --> 00:30:42,396
DIANE: Not everyone gets
a second chance.

734
00:30:42,532 --> 00:30:46,600
Make the most of it,
Mr. Poodleton.

735
00:30:50,302 --> 00:30:51,641
(engine starts)

736
00:30:51,776 --> 00:30:54,013
(sirens wailing)

737
00:30:55,113 --> 00:30:57,307
-(chuckles)
-SNAKE: Wolf?

738
00:30:57,443 --> 00:30:58,619
What are you doing?

739
00:30:58,754 --> 00:31:00,178
-WOLF: What?
-OTHERS: Yeah.

740
00:31:00,314 --> 00:31:02,252
Oh, that. (chuckles)

741
00:31:02,388 --> 00:31:05,083
I-I-I'm sorry.
I thought it was, uh, obvious.

742
00:31:05,219 --> 00:31:07,256
We're gonna go good.

743
