or too gutless
to take advantage of it.

993
00:40:09,227 --> 00:40:10,995
Gutless? I'm gutless?

994
00:40:11,131 --> 00:40:12,226
(chuckles):
Oh.

995
00:40:12,362 --> 00:40:13,758
I'm sorry, have we met?

996
00:40:13,893 --> 00:40:15,230
I'm the villain of every story.

997
00:40:15,366 --> 00:40:16,596
Guilty until proven innocent.

998
00:40:16,731 --> 00:40:19,828
Even if by some miracle
we did change,

999
00:40:19,963 --> 00:40:21,670
who's gonna believe us, huh?

1000
00:40:21,805 --> 00:40:23,605
Of course you wouldn't know
anything about that,

1001
00:40:23,740 --> 00:40:27,609
with your Little Miss Perfect
power suits.

1002
00:40:28,605 --> 00:40:29,812
Is that so?

1003
00:40:29,948 --> 00:40:31,409
Wait a second.

1004
00:40:31,545 --> 00:40:33,206
What did... How did you...

1005
00:40:33,342 --> 00:40:37,578
A wolf and a fox
are not so different.

1006
00:40:38,381 --> 00:40:40,715
Maybe they will believe you,
maybe they won't,

1007
00:40:40,850 --> 00:40:42,213
but it doesn't matter.

1008
00:40:42,349 --> 00:40:44,655
Don't do it for them.
Do it for you.

1009
00:40:44,791 --> 00:40:47,287
This is a chance
to write your own story.

1010
00:40:47,422 --> 00:40:50,389
To find a better life for you
and your friends.

1011
00:40:51,192 --> 00:40:52,957
Come on,
what have you got to lose?

1012
00:40:53,093 --> 00:40:55,062
I don't know. My dignity?

1013
00:40:56,231 --> 00:40:59,638
Yeah, well,
that ship has already sailed.

1014
00:41:05,615 --> 00:41:08,406
Believe it or not,
I'm rooting for you, Wolf.

1015
00:41:09,209 --> 00:41:11,377
So you're not gonna
call the chief?

1016
00:41:12,180 --> 00:41:15,081
-I'll see you at the gala.
-(engine starts)

1017
00:41:16,254 --> 00:41:18,491
♪ ♪

1018
00:41:32,997 --> 00:41:34,703
(cat meows in distance)

1019
00:41:36,175 --> 00:41:38,707
(meowing continues)

1020
00:41:48,051 --> 00:41:49,715
(meows)

1021
00:41:49,850 --> 00:41:52,218
I think we got off
to a bad start.

1022
00:41:52,353 --> 00:41:54,348
The name's Wolf.

1023
00:41:55,125 --> 00:41:56,893
(whimpers)

1024
00:41:57,028 --> 00:41:58,720
Yep. (sighs)

1025
00:41:58,855 --> 00:42:00,195
I get that a lot.

1026
00:42:00,331 --> 00:42:02,557
First impressions and all.

1027
00:42:02,692 --> 00:42:04,526
(whimpers)

1028
00:42:04,662 --> 00:42:06,057
(meows, yowls)

1029
00:42:06,193 --> 00:42:07,833
No, no, no, no. (whimpers)

1030
00:42:09,765 --> 00:42:10,871
(panting)

1031
00:42:11,007 --> 00:42:12,574
(sighs)

1032
00:42:14,310 --> 00:42:15,972
Uh, it's okay. It's okay.

1033
00:42:16,107 --> 00:42:18,037
I'm not gonna hurt you.
I know you're scared.

1034
00:42:18,172 --> 00:42:20,273
I would be, too, if I were you.

1035
00:42:21,217 --> 00:42:22,774
Just give me a chance.

1036
00:42:22,909 --> 00:42:24,046
(meows quietly)

1037
00:42:24,181 --> 00:42:27,152
Truth is we actually have
a lot in common.

1038
00:42:27,287 --> 00:42:29,156
Don't tell anyone,

1039
00:42:29,291 --> 00:42:32,016
but I love a little scratch

1040
00:42:32,151 --> 00:42:34,325
on the spot behind my ears.

1041
00:42:34,460 --> 00:42:36,160
You know, right there.

1042
00:42:36,295 --> 00:42:38,356
The best.

1043
00:42:39,726 --> 00:42:41,534
(meows)

1044
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:45,736
Come on, kitty.

1045
00:42:46,733 --> 00:42:48,303
(sniffing)

1046
00:42:48,439 --> 00:42:50,774
(meows, purrs)

1047
00:42:56,207 --> 00:42:58,440
-♪ ♪
-(purring)

1048
00:43:03,622 --> 00:43:05,953
-Yeah. Who's a good kitty?
-(meows)

1049
00:43:06,088 --> 00:43:07,981
-Who's a good kitty?
-TARANTULA: Uh, Wolf?

1050
00:43:08,116 --> 00:43:10,919
Um, you saved him?

1051
00:43:11,054 --> 00:43:12,319
MARMALADE:
Yes!

1052
00:43:12,454 --> 00:43:15,395
(chuckling):
Yes. It's working.

1053
00:43:15,531 --> 00:43:16,764
You-you filmed that?

1054
00:43:16,900 --> 00:43:19,335
Yes, and they're starting
to like you.

1055
00:43:19,470 --> 00:43:20,501
SHARK (chuckling):
Yeah!

1056
00:43:20,636 --> 00:43:22,369
-All right!
-(whooping)

1057
00:43:22,505 --> 00:43:23,637
This might just be enough

1058
00:43:23,773 --> 00:43:25,101
to win over the guests
at the gala.

1059
00:43:25,237 --> 00:43:27,202
-Now we're talking!
-Yes! -All right!

1060
00:43:27,338 --> 00:43:29,937
TARANTULA:
Yeah, we did it! All right!

1061
00:43:30,073 --> 00:43:31,713
MARMALADE:
Uh, Wolf?

1062
00:43:31,848 --> 00:43:34,240
I must say,
you've really turned a corner.

1063
00:43:34,375 --> 00:43:36,250
-You're really getting it.
-Really?

1064
00:43:36,386 --> 00:43:37,953
-Oh, uh, thanks.
-(meows)

1065
00:43:38,088 --> 00:43:39,113
Now, I mean it.

1066
00:43:39,249 --> 00:43:41,189
And I can see it
from tip to tail.

1067
00:43:41,959 --> 00:43:45,486
It's just a shame that you
have to carry all that baggage.

1068
00:43:46,355 --> 00:43:48,854
What are you talk...
You mean the guys?

1069
00:43:48,989 --> 00:43:50,256
What do you mean?

1070
00:43:50,392 --> 00:43:51,765
MARMALADE:
You have great potential, Wolf,

1071
00:43:51,900 --> 00:43:53,358
but at some point,
you're going to have to choose

1072
00:43:53,494 --> 00:43:56,637
between your friends
or the good life.

1073
00:44:00,801 --> 00:44:02,840
(snoring)

1074
00:44:05,511 --> 00:44:07,673
Hey. You still awake?

1075
00:44:07,808 --> 00:44:09,348
(cat meows)

1076
00:44:09,483 --> 00:44:11,044
You-you brought the cat in?

1077
00:44:11,179 --> 00:44:12,882
(chuckling):
Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

1078
00:44:13,017 --> 00:44:14,943
I'm just...
I'm just saving it up for later.

1079
00:44:15,078 --> 00:44:16,480
Why? What's up?

1080
00:44:17,317 --> 00:44:18,950
I was just getting
a little worried,

1081
00:44:19,085 --> 00:44:20,754
since you've kind of become a...

1082
00:44:20,890 --> 00:44:22,853
-Become a what?
-(purring)

1083
00:44:22,989 --> 00:44:25,021
You know, teacher's pet.

1084
00:44:25,156 --> 00:44:27,355
Getting all cozy with Marmalade.

1085
00:44:27,490 --> 00:44:29,458
Your tail wagging
and everything.

1086
00:44:29,593 --> 00:44:31,565
Well, yeah, because
it has to be believable.

1087
00:44:31,701 --> 00:44:34,429
Uh-huh. Yeah, I guess so.

1088
00:44:34,565 --> 00:44:37,170
As long as it's all
part of the plan.

1089
00:44:38,040 --> 00:44:40,600
It is all part of the plan,
isn't it?

1090
00:44:40,735 --> 00:44:43,880
Snake, buddy,
who made the plan to begin with?

1091
00:44:44,016 --> 00:44:45,409
You did.

1092
00:44:45,545 --> 00:44:49,015
So I'm the one who sticks
to the plan the most, right?

1093
00:44:50,653 --> 00:44:52,212
Yeah, ri... Uh, yeah, ok...

1094
00:44:52,347 --> 00:44:54,589
I guess that makes sense, yeah.

1095
00:44:54,725 --> 00:44:57,117
But if the plan
were ever to change,

1096
00:44:57,252 --> 00:44:59,959
you'd-you'd tell me, right?

1097
00:45:02,464 --> 00:45:04,593
You have my word.

1098
00:45:04,728 --> 00:45:06,767
Go bad...

1099
00:45:07,566 --> 00:45:09,462
Or go home.

1100
00:45:17,306 --> 00:45:19,480
-Hey, Snake. -Yeah?
-(purring)

1101
00:45:19,615 --> 00:45:21,815
You ever wonder
what it'd be like?

1102
00:45:21,951 --> 00:45:24,618
The world loving us
instead of being scared of us?

1103
00:45:24,754 --> 00:45:26,647
You ever...
you ever think about that?

1104
00:45:26,782 --> 00:45:27,913
Loving us?

1105
00:45:28,049 --> 00:45:29,447
(chuckles) Yeah, right.

1106
00:45:29,583 --> 00:45:31,521
I don't waste time
thinking about stuff

1107
00:45:31,657 --> 00:45:33,188
that's never gonna happen.

1108
00:45:33,323 --> 00:45:37,730
(sighs) I can't wait for things
to get back to normal.

1109
00:45:44,771 --> 00:45:47,365
Yeah. Back to normal,
back to normal.

1110
00:45:48,405 --> 00:45:50,401
(sighs)

1111
00:45:51,643 --> 00:45:53,745
(dramatic news theme plays)

1112
00:45:55,879 --> 00:45:58,375
What up?
We are just moments away

1113
00:45:58,511 --> 00:46:00,410
from Professor Marmalade's
Gala for Goodness,

1114
00:46:00,545 --> 00:46:02,576
where the legendary
Love Crater Meteorite

1115
00:46:02,712 --> 00:46:05,722
will be on display
for the first time ever.

1116
00:46:05,858 --> 00:46:08,485
But what everyone
is really buzzing about

1117
00:46:08,620 --> 00:46:11,958
is the Bad Guys, whose
heart-melting rescue video

1118
00:46:12,094 --> 00:46:15,930
has made them an overnight
viral sensation.

1119
00:46:17,362 --> 00:46:19,400
All right, guys,
this is the big one.

1120
00:46:19,535 --> 00:46:21,129
The Golden Dolphin

1121
00:46:21,265 --> 00:46:22,731
<i>is inside a titanium case</i>

1122
00:46:22,866 --> 00:46:24,704
<i>controlled by a randomly</i>
<i>generated five-digit code,</i>

1123
00:46:24,839 --> 00:46:26,371
<i>a code kept safe and secure</i>

1124
00:46:26,506 --> 00:46:29,402
<i>inside a briefcase handcuffed</i>
<i>to the chief of police.</i>

1125
00:46:29,538 --> 00:46:31,406
PIRANHA:
<i>She's not messing around.</i>

1126
00:46:31,541 --> 00:46:33,115
WOLF:<i> The code is only</i>
<i>accessible with</i>

1127
00:46:33,250 --> 00:46:34,848
<i>-her authorized fingerprints.</i>
-SNAKE:<i> Leave that to me.</i>

1128
00:46:34,983 --> 00:46:36,916
WOLF:
<i>While Snake gets the code,</i>

1129
00:46:37,052 --> 00:46:38,411
<i>Shark will secure</i>
<i>the fake Dolphin.</i>

1130
00:46:38,546 --> 00:46:40,152
SHARK:
<i>I like the sound of that.</i>

1131
00:46:40,288 --> 00:46:42,022
WOLF:<i> Meanwhile, the rest of us</i>
<i>plant circuit jammers.</i>

1132
00:46:42,158 --> 00:46:44,124
TARANTULA:<i> Allowing me</i>
<i>to hack into the power grid.</i>

1133
00:46:44,259 --> 00:46:45,823
WOLF:<i> At the end of the night,</i>
<i>we toast the professor,</i>

1134
00:46:45,958 --> 00:46:47,862
<i>"Blah-blah-blah, yada yada,"</i>

1135
00:46:47,997 --> 00:46:50,392
<i>and when I say "Marmalade,"</i>
<i>lights go out,</i>

1136
00:46:50,527 --> 00:46:53,325
<i>and we'll have exactly</i>
<i>four seconds to make our move.</i>

1137
00:46:53,460 --> 00:46:55,364
SNAKE:
<i>The old switcheroo.</i>

1138
00:46:55,500 --> 00:46:58,171
WOLF:<i> Chief hands Marmalade</i>
<i>the fake Dolphin,</i>

1139
00:46:58,306 --> 00:47:01,271
<i>we get our pardon, applause,</i>
<i>applause, exit stage right,</i>

1140
00:47:01,406 --> 00:47:03,873
<i>and by the time they realize</i>
<i>what happened...</i>

1141
00:47:04,009 --> 00:47:05,569
(over speakers):
So long, suckers!

1142
00:47:05,705 --> 00:47:07,345
<i>...we'll be driving off</i>
<i>into the sunset,</i>

1143
00:47:07,481 --> 00:47:08,647
<i>legacy cemented.</i>

1144
00:47:08,783 --> 00:47:10,108
<i>-(laughter)</i>
-PIRANHA:<i> Nice.</i>

1145
00:47:10,244 --> 00:47:11,515
Got to hand it to you, buddy.

1146
00:47:11,650 --> 00:47:13,577
You're a real artist.

1147
00:47:16,182 --> 00:47:18,113
Well, Good Guys, this is it.

1148
00:47:18,249 --> 00:47:19,649
Good luck out there.

1149
00:47:19,784 --> 00:47:23,626
Remember, all eyes will be
on you tonight, not me.

1150
00:47:23,761 --> 00:47:27,623
Friends, meet the Good Guys!

1151
00:47:28,895 --> 00:47:30,867
(cheering)

1152
00:47:33,329 --> 00:47:35,332
Uh, this is different.

1153
00:47:35,468 --> 00:47:37,432
-Is this a prank?
-What's that sound?

1154
00:47:37,568 --> 00:47:39,633
Like screaming
but not terrified.

1155
00:47:39,769 --> 00:47:42,609
All right, guys,
let's, uh... let's mingle.

1156
00:47:42,744 --> 00:47:44,913
It's crime time, baby.

1157
00:47:45,781 --> 00:47:47,014
♪ Fly me to the moon ♪

1158
00:47:47,149 --> 00:47:49,409
♪ And let me play
among the stars ♪

1159
00:47:49,544 --> 00:47:50,952
-Hmm?
-MAN: There you go.

1160
00:47:51,087 --> 00:47:53,147
♪ Let me see
what spring is like ♪

1161
00:47:53,283 --> 00:47:55,523
♪ On Jupiter and Mars ♪

1162
00:47:55,658 --> 00:47:57,024
♪ In other words... ♪

1163
00:47:57,159 --> 00:47:59,226
Okay, fake Dolphin,
fake Dolphin, fake Dolphin.

1164
00:47:59,361 --> 00:48:00,551
Bingo.

1165
00:48:00,687 --> 00:48:02,689
-Mr. Shark, Mr. Shark!
-Ooh!

1166
00:48:02,824 --> 00:48:05,091
Is it true sharks
can smell blood a mile away?

1167
00:48:05,227 --> 00:48:07,360
What? No. That's freaky.

1168
00:48:07,495 --> 00:48:09,336
♪ Fill my heart with song ♪

1169
00:48:09,471 --> 00:48:10,838
(Snake chuckling)

1170
00:48:10,973 --> 00:48:12,873
♪ And let me sing
forevermore... ♪

1171
00:48:13,008 --> 00:48:14,739
-Oh, Mr. Wolf! Mr. Wolf!
-(chuckling): Hey. Whoa.

1172
00:48:14,875 --> 00:48:16,206
It is a pleasure to meet you.

1173
00:48:16,341 --> 00:48:18,138
-Pleasure is all mine.
-I loved your video.

1174
00:48:18,273 --> 00:48:20,079
Can I get a picture for my kids?

1175
00:48:20,215 --> 00:48:22,614
Uh, hey, just a minute, guys.
Let me... let me, uh...

1176
00:48:22,749 --> 00:48:25,047
I got... I'll be right back.

1177
00:48:25,183 --> 00:48:27,345
♪ In other words,
I love you... ♪

1178
00:48:27,480 --> 00:48:31,583
Okay, Wolf, what are you up to?

1179
00:48:32,551 --> 00:48:34,586
Yeah, with criminals like this,

1180
00:48:34,721 --> 00:48:38,062
you got to be crafty,
subtle, invisible.

1181
00:48:38,197 --> 00:48:41,532
And then the moment
they let their guard down...

1182
00:48:41,668 --> 00:48:43,633
-whammo!
-(groans)

1183
00:48:43,769 --> 00:48:44,967
You gotta spring the trap!

1184
00:48:45,103 --> 00:48:47,530
(chuckling):
Always one step ahead.

1185
00:48:47,665 --> 00:48:50,167
I think I've earned
a tonic water.

1186
00:48:50,302 --> 00:48:52,474
Put it in a fun glass, huh?

1187
00:48:52,609 --> 00:48:54,402
Oh! Nice.

1188
00:48:54,537 --> 00:48:56,270
-(Snake groans)
-(gasps)

1189
00:48:56,405 --> 00:48:58,007
-Oh, no.
-(gasps)

1190
00:48:58,142 --> 00:48:59,917
Hey. (stammers)

1191
00:49:01,418 --> 00:49:03,084
(gasps)

1192
00:49:04,515 --> 00:49:06,388
-(chuckles nervously)
-Hey.

1193
00:49:06,524 --> 00:49:08,020
That's right.

1194
00:49:08,156 --> 00:49:10,190
-Be intimidated.
-(Snake groans)

1195
00:49:11,329 --> 00:49:12,896
Mm.

1196
00:49:14,556 --> 00:49:15,888
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

1197
00:49:16,023 --> 00:49:20,529
-♪ Look... at me ♪
-(guests murmuring)

1198
00:49:23,332 --> 00:49:24,403
-What?
-Hmm?

1199
00:49:24,539 --> 00:49:26,301
(groans)

1200
00:49:26,436 --> 00:49:32,177
♪ Tell me what... you see ♪

1201
00:49:34,607 --> 00:49:39,486
♪ Am I good... or bad? ♪

1202
00:49:39,622 --> 00:49:40,684
(chuckles nervously)

1203
00:49:40,820 --> 00:49:42,546
(record scratching)

1204
00:49:42,682 --> 00:49:48,328
♪ Don't you judge... so fast ♪

1205
00:49:48,463 --> 00:49:50,129
(cheering)

1206
00:49:50,265 --> 00:49:52,966
♪ Hey, hey, hey,
I know you think you know me ♪

1207
00:49:53,101 --> 00:49:54,800
♪ You've made
your own conclusion ♪

1208
00:49:54,935 --> 00:49:56,960
♪ You think that I look scary ♪

1209
00:49:57,096 --> 00:49:58,134
(groans)

1210
00:49:58,269 --> 00:50:00,365
♪ Well, that's
your own delusion ♪

1211
00:50:00,500 --> 00:50:01,941
♪ Listen when I tell you ♪

1212
00:50:02,076 --> 00:50:03,976
♪ There's more
than meets the eye ♪

1213
00:50:04,112 --> 00:50:06,041
-♪ So take a closer look ♪
-(groans)

1214
00:50:06,176 --> 00:50:08,713
♪ To find a real good guy ♪

1215
00:50:08,849 --> 00:50:11,108
♪ We're not the Bad Guys... ♪

1216
00:50:11,244 --> 00:50:12,243
DIANE:
Mr. Wolf.

1217
00:50:12,379 --> 00:50:14,049
Diane. Yeah, what a surprise.

1218
00:50:14,184 --> 00:50:15,644
You know,
if I didn't know better,

1219
00:50:15,780 --> 00:50:17,179
I'd think that
you were avoiding me.

1220
00:50:17,315 --> 00:50:18,522
Avoiding you?

1221
00:50:18,658 --> 00:50:20,320
Wh-Why would I do that?

1222
00:50:21,316 --> 00:50:22,685
Okay.

1223
00:50:22,821 --> 00:50:26,363
But I have to say,
I'm a little disappointed.

1224
00:50:27,166 --> 00:50:30,123
I was hoping you were gonna
ask me to dance.

1225
00:50:30,259 --> 00:50:31,458
Oh.

1226
00:50:31,594 --> 00:50:33,034
♪ Get up on the floor ♪

1227
00:50:33,168 --> 00:50:35,101
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1228
00:50:35,236 --> 00:50:37,169
♪ Wanna get you feeling right ♪

1229
00:50:37,304 --> 00:50:39,698
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1230
00:50:39,834 --> 00:50:41,470
♪ We're the Good, Good Guys ♪

1231
00:50:41,605 --> 00:50:43,736
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1232
00:50:43,871 --> 00:50:45,507
♪ Wanna get you feeling right ♪

1233
00:50:45,642 --> 00:50:47,672
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1234
00:50:47,808 --> 00:50:50,310
♪ We're the Good, Good Guys ♪

1235
00:50:50,446 --> 00:50:52,250
♪ Come on! Ooh... ♪

1236
00:50:52,385 --> 00:50:55,190
I see.
You lost the sheep's clothing.

1237
00:50:55,326 --> 00:50:58,223
Yeah. Figured it was time I got
comfortable in my own fur.

1238
00:50:58,359 --> 00:50:59,993
PIRANHA: If you're
feeling good in here...

1239
00:51:00,129 --> 00:51:02,462
I said, if you're feeling
good in here...

1240
00:51:02,597 --> 00:51:04,157
(laughter)

1241
00:51:04,292 --> 00:51:05,358
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1242
00:51:05,493 --> 00:51:06,898
I think I like the new you.

1243
00:51:07,033 --> 00:51:08,465
Well, that makes two of us.

1244
00:51:08,600 --> 00:51:13,205
♪ We're all here to have
a good, good time ♪

1245
00:51:13,341 --> 00:51:17,100
♪ Let the rhythm move you
and open up your mind ♪

1246
00:51:17,235 --> 00:51:22,005
♪ Next time you see me
in your neighborhood ♪

1247
00:51:22,141 --> 00:51:25,645
♪ Don't you be thinking
that I'm up to no good ♪

1248
00:51:25,780 --> 00:51:29,747
♪ I just want you
to give me a chance ♪

1249
00:51:29,883 --> 00:51:33,649
♪ I know your body
really wants to dance ♪

1250
00:51:33,785 --> 00:51:35,524
♪ So leave your judgments... ♪

1251
00:51:35,659 --> 00:51:38,922
Break out the umbrellas,
because it's raining money.

1252
00:51:39,058 --> 00:51:41,490
All because of-- I can't even
believe I'm saying this--

1253
00:51:41,625 --> 00:51:44,231
all because of the Bad Guys.

1254
00:51:44,366 --> 00:51:46,167
♪ Wanna get you feeling right ♪

1255
00:51:46,302 --> 00:51:47,970
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1256
00:51:48,106 --> 00:51:49,973
♪ We're the Good, Good Guys ♪

1257
00:51:50,108 --> 00:51:52,568
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1258
00:51:52,703 --> 00:51:54,504
♪ Wanna get you feeling right ♪

1259
00:51:54,639 --> 00:51:56,409
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1260
00:51:56,545 --> 00:51:59,472
♪ We're the Good,
Good Guys, whoo... ♪

1261
00:51:59,608 --> 00:52:01,347
So, how does it feel

1262
00:52:01,483 --> 00:52:04,185
to have everyone
not fear you for a change?

1263
00:52:04,320 --> 00:52:06,847
-(panting)
-(music continues muffled)

1264
00:52:07,658 --> 00:52:09,388
(muffled cheering)

1265
00:52:11,926 --> 00:52:14,397
It feels good.

1266
00:52:14,532 --> 00:52:15,990
Real good.

1267
00:52:16,126 --> 00:52:17,726
Diane...

1268
00:52:19,669 --> 00:52:21,228
(gasps softly)

1269
00:52:21,363 --> 00:52:23,197
It belongs to you.

1270
00:52:23,332 --> 00:52:25,131
(music unmuffles)

1271
00:52:25,266 --> 00:52:26,666
-♪ We're gonna be
good tonight ♪ -♪ Uh-huh ♪

1272
00:52:26,801 --> 00:52:28,309
♪ We're gonna be good tonight ♪

1273
00:52:28,444 --> 00:52:31,379
♪ Ah, one, two, three,
we're the Good, Good Guys ♪

1274
00:52:31,514 --> 00:52:34,046
-♪ We're gonna be
good tonight ♪ -♪ So good ♪

1275
00:52:34,181 --> 00:52:36,108
♪ Gonna get you feeling right ♪

1276
00:52:36,244 --> 00:52:38,181
-♪ We're gonna be
good tonight ♪ -♪ So good ♪

1277
00:52:38,317 --> 00:52:40,785
♪ We're the Good, Good Guys ♪

1278
00:52:40,920 --> 00:52:45,683
♪ Oh, yeah... ♪

1279
00:52:45,819 --> 00:52:47,951
-(song ends)
-(cheering and applause)

1280
00:52:49,527 --> 00:52:51,523
(sound of fireworks whistling
and exploding)

1281
00:52:51,658 --> 00:52:53,328
Thank you. Thank you, Mr. Wolf.

1282
00:52:53,464 --> 00:52:55,025
As you know,
the money raised tonight

1283
00:52:55,160 --> 00:52:58,168
will be delivered tomorrow
to schools, hospitals

1284
00:52:58,303 --> 00:53:00,329
and other worthy causes
across the city.

1285
00:53:00,464 --> 00:53:01,563
(cheering)

1286
00:53:01,698 --> 00:53:03,867
Uh... (clears throat)

1287
00:53:04,002 --> 00:53:07,035
I just want to take
a moment to recognize

1288
00:53:07,170 --> 00:53:09,307
the one responsible
for our new outlook.

1289
00:53:09,442 --> 00:53:11,941
Our brilliant mentor,

1290
00:53:12,076 --> 00:53:13,676
-a paragon of enlightenment...
-Do it. -Come on.

1291
00:53:13,812 --> 00:53:16,813
...the one and only
Professor...

1292
00:53:19,457 --> 00:53:21,622
-TARANTULA: Wolf, do it.
-WOLF: ...uh, Professor...

1293
00:53:21,758 --> 00:53:23,019
(hisses)

1294
00:53:23,155 --> 00:53:25,359
...um...

1295
00:53:27,194 --> 00:53:29,323
...Professor Marmalade!

1296
00:53:29,458 --> 00:53:31,134
(cheering)

1297
00:53:32,002 --> 00:53:34,269
Chief, may I do the honors?

1298
00:53:37,434 --> 00:53:38,563
That's not the plan.

1299
00:53:38,698 --> 00:53:39,739
What is happening?

1300
00:53:39,874 --> 00:53:41,275
He's gone rogue.

1301
00:53:42,745 --> 00:53:44,575
A deal's a deal.

1302
00:53:45,612 --> 00:53:48,446
By the power vested in me,
it is a pleasure

1303
00:53:48,581 --> 00:53:51,082
to grant the Bad Guys
a full par...

1304
00:53:51,217 --> 00:53:53,451
(guests gasping, murmuring)

1305
00:53:55,115 --> 00:53:57,691
-That was weird.
-MAN: The meteorite is gone!

1306
00:53:57,826 --> 00:53:59,193
Somebody stole it!

1307
00:54:01,755 --> 00:54:03,160
-(chief groans)
-Chief.

1308
00:54:03,296 --> 00:54:05,164
-Wolf. (growls)
-Come on.

1309
00:54:05,300 --> 00:54:06,923
You can't possibly think
that we did this.

1310
00:54:07,059 --> 00:54:09,268
(over speakers):
So long, suckers!

1311
00:54:10,363 --> 00:54:11,769
Run!

1312
00:54:11,904 --> 00:54:13,232
Get them!

1313
00:54:13,367 --> 00:54:15,868
(clamoring)

1314
00:54:20,637 --> 00:54:22,982
Uh... (chuckles)

1315
00:54:23,117 --> 00:54:25,415
-(panting)
-(officers grunting)

1316
00:54:26,687 --> 00:54:28,352
Here. Here.

1317
00:54:28,487 --> 00:54:31,048
-What are you doing?
-I'm giving it all back.

1318
00:54:31,184 --> 00:54:32,286
Huh?

1319
00:54:32,421 --> 00:54:34,483
-(clamoring)
-Excuse me.

1320
00:54:34,619 --> 00:54:36,659
(panting, grunting)

1321
00:54:37,529 --> 00:54:40,021
-What happened back there?
-I couldn't do it.

1322
00:54:40,157 --> 00:54:41,900
What do you mean,
you couldn't do it?

1323
00:54:42,035 --> 00:54:43,298
-I-I-I just... I...
-No!

1324
00:54:43,434 --> 00:54:45,735
-I do not run.
-OFFICERS: Hut, hut, hut...

1325
00:54:45,871 --> 00:54:47,531
That is not how I roll.

1326
00:54:47,666 --> 00:54:49,463
Piranha,
don't do anything crazy.

1327
00:54:49,598 --> 00:54:50,934
(laughing)

1328
00:54:51,069 --> 00:54:54,376
Crazy is what I bring
to the party,<i> chico.</i>

1329
00:54:58,706 --> 00:55:00,876
(Shark groans)

1330
00:55:02,251 --> 00:55:03,619
Hey, you're making a mistake.

1331
00:55:03,754 --> 00:55:04,710
We didn't do it.

1332
00:55:04,846 --> 00:55:05,978
I know we always say that,

1333
00:55:06,114 --> 00:55:07,186
but this time
it's actually true.

1334
00:55:07,322 --> 00:55:09,192
A-la-la-la-la. Can't hear you.

1335
00:55:09,326 --> 00:55:11,422
-Guilty, guilty, guilty.
-Talk to Marmalade.

1336
00:55:11,558 --> 00:55:13,353
We're really good now.
He'll tell you.

1337
00:55:13,488 --> 00:55:14,592
Professor!

1338
00:55:14,727 --> 00:55:16,990
Tonight's headline:
Change is impossible.

1339
00:55:17,125 --> 00:55:18,992
You should always judge
a book by its cover,

1340
00:55:19,127 --> 00:55:21,367
and all stereotypes
have been affirmed.

1341
00:55:21,502 --> 00:55:23,100
MARMALADE:
Stop, for goodness' sake!

1342
00:55:23,235 --> 00:55:24,535
Let me speak to them.

1343
00:55:24,671 --> 00:55:27,200
I'm-I'm sure there's been
some misunderstanding.

1344
00:55:28,003 --> 00:55:30,139
-(door opens)
-Ah, Professor Marmalade.

1345
00:55:30,275 --> 00:55:31,635
You've got five minutes.

1346
00:55:31,771 --> 00:55:33,781
No deals this time.

1347
00:55:33,916 --> 00:55:34,940
Y-You have to help us.

1348
00:55:35,075 --> 00:55:36,612
Tell 'em.
Tell 'em we didn't do it.

1349
00:55:36,747 --> 00:55:38,607
There, there.
Of course you didn't do it.

1350
00:55:38,743 --> 00:55:39,877
How could you?

1351
00:55:40,012 --> 00:55:43,388
After all,
you're such a good boy.

1352
00:55:44,189 --> 00:55:47,551
You're such a good boy.

1353
00:55:47,687 --> 00:55:49,387
That shiver up my spine.

1354
00:55:49,523 --> 00:55:51,762
The wag in my tiny tail.

1355
00:55:51,897 --> 00:55:53,122
Arrest them!

1356
00:55:53,258 --> 00:55:55,023
What if we tried
a little experiment, Diane?

1357
00:55:55,159 --> 00:55:57,468
As you know,
my Gala for Goodness...

1358
00:55:57,604 --> 00:55:59,831
TIFFANY: Where the legendary
Love Crater Meteorite

1359
00:55:59,967 --> 00:56:02,503
will be on display
for the first time ever.

1360
00:56:02,638 --> 00:56:05,936
All eyes will be
on you tonight, not me.

1361
00:56:06,772 --> 00:56:08,012
WOMAN:
<i>You're such a...</i>

1362
00:56:08,147 --> 00:56:10,446
MARMALADE:
<i>Good boy.</i>

1363
00:56:11,442 --> 00:56:12,848
You.

1364
00:56:12,983 --> 00:56:14,547
It was all you.

1365
00:56:14,683 --> 00:56:16,075
What are you talking about,
Wolf?

1366
00:56:16,211 --> 00:56:17,484
The old lady,
the Golden Dolphin,

1367
00:56:17,620 --> 00:56:19,346
good training--
it was all to get us here,

1368
00:56:19,482 --> 00:56:21,715
so he could steal the meteorite
and let us take the fall.

1369
00:56:21,851 --> 00:56:23,525
Whoa. Whoa, what old lady?

1370
00:56:23,661 --> 00:56:26,159
And-and why would a guinea pig
want a meteorite anyway?

1371
00:56:26,294 --> 00:56:29,064
(Marmalade chuckling)

1372
00:56:29,199 --> 00:56:32,000
Uh, guys, he's creeping me out.

1373
00:56:32,135 --> 00:56:33,725
Wait, what? What's going on?

1374
00:56:33,861 --> 00:56:35,135
Someone turn me around.

1375
00:56:35,271 --> 00:56:36,904
MARMALADE:
Well, well.

1376
00:56:37,040 --> 00:56:38,939
So, you finally get it.

1377
00:56:39,075 --> 00:56:40,468
-Wait.
-What?

1378
00:56:40,604 --> 00:56:42,075
You stole the meteorite?

1379
00:56:42,211 --> 00:56:44,176
Oh, it's not just a meteorite.

1380
00:56:44,311 --> 00:56:45,746
I told you guys it's a butt.

1381
00:56:45,881 --> 00:56:47,078
It's not a butt!

1382
00:56:47,214 --> 00:56:48,412
(takes deep breath)

1383
00:56:48,547 --> 00:56:51,011
It's the ultimate power source.

1384
00:56:51,146 --> 00:56:54,013
You see, when it struck,
scientists found that

1385
00:56:54,149 --> 00:56:55,879
it emitted
an electromagnetic frequency

1386
00:56:56,015 --> 00:56:57,947
unlike anything else on Earth.

1387
00:56:58,083 --> 00:56:59,756
I'm going to harness its power

1388
00:56:59,892 --> 00:57:03,092
to pull off the greatest heist
the world has ever seen.

1389
00:57:03,895 --> 00:57:05,822
You should've eaten him
when you had the chance.

1390
00:57:05,958 --> 00:57:07,431
-Yep.
-But why us?

1391
00:57:07,567 --> 00:57:09,798
Because you're
the perfect patsies.

1392
00:57:09,933 --> 00:57:13,405
Come on, when people look up
"bad" in the dictionary,

1393
00:57:13,540 --> 00:57:16,006
do they see a sweet,
adorable guinea pig?

1394
00:57:16,141 --> 00:57:18,009
No. They see you.

1395
00:57:18,144 --> 00:57:20,372
And they always will.

1396
00:57:20,507 --> 00:57:21,769
Okay, fine.

1397
00:57:21,904 --> 00:57:23,180
But you set us up.

1398
00:57:23,315 --> 00:57:24,580
(chuckling):
Oh, pish-pish.

1399
00:57:24,715 --> 00:57:27,548
Let's be honest--
evolution set you up.

1400
00:57:27,684 --> 00:57:29,880
But Wolfie here
really clinched it.

1401
00:57:30,016 --> 00:57:32,820
You fell for every one
of my traps,

1402
00:57:32,955 --> 00:57:36,752
starting with saving
a helpless little old lady.

1403
00:57:36,888 --> 00:57:40,056
Wolf, what's he talking about?

1404
00:57:42,331 --> 00:57:43,867
MARMALADE:
Whoops.

1405
00:57:44,003 --> 00:57:46,729
Did I say too much?

1406
00:57:46,865 --> 00:57:49,197
Anyhoo, looks like, yet again,

1407
00:57:49,332 --> 00:57:52,965
the Big Bad Wolf got outsmarted
by a little piggy.

1408
00:57:53,101 --> 00:57:55,935
You little pouchy-cheeked rat!

1409
00:57:56,070 --> 00:57:57,479
I'll kill you! You hear me?

1410
00:57:57,615 --> 00:57:59,742
-You're dead! You're de...
-Help! Help! Help!

1411
00:57:59,877 --> 00:58:01,513
The Big Bad Wolf
is attacking me.

1412
00:58:01,649 --> 00:58:04,177
Oh, now you are done
forever, Wolf!

1413
00:58:09,293 --> 00:58:12,086
-(engine revs)
-(sirens wailing)

1414
00:58:13,420 --> 00:58:15,253
-(Marmalade whimpering)
-TIFFANY: Professor, Professor,

1415
00:58:15,388 --> 00:58:17,330
any thoughts
on how the Bad Guys managed

1416
00:58:17,466 --> 00:58:19,858
to steal the meteorite
in plain sight?

1417
00:58:19,994 --> 00:58:21,226
Well, off the top of my head,

1418
00:58:21,361 --> 00:58:23,103
perhaps they accessed the site
previously

1419
00:58:23,239 --> 00:58:24,505
and set up an intricate system

1420
00:58:24,640 --> 00:58:26,166
-of tunnels and trapdoors...
-TIFFANY: Uh-huh.

1421
00:58:26,301 --> 00:58:27,639
MARMALADE: ...that could be
remotely triggered

1422
00:58:27,774 --> 00:58:29,232
to suck the meteorite down
into a holding area,

1423
00:58:29,368 --> 00:58:30,941
-but how should I know?
-TIFFANY: Totally.

1424
00:58:31,077 --> 00:58:33,809
MARMALADE: I mean, they're the
deranged masterminds, not me.

1425
00:58:56,028 --> 00:58:58,502
WOLF:
<i>I'm giving it all back.</i>

1426
00:59:00,633 --> 00:59:02,499
(wind howling)

1427
00:59:02,634 --> 00:59:04,673
♪ ♪

1428
00:59:22,352 --> 00:59:24,091
SHARK: I can't believe
we got double-crossed

1429
00:59:24,226 --> 00:59:25,527
by a tiny rodent.

1430
00:59:25,663 --> 00:59:27,988
Oh, we got double-crossed
by a rodent all right,

1431
00:59:28,124 --> 00:59:30,829
-but, uh, not a tiny one.
-What?

1432
00:59:30,964 --> 00:59:33,466
This was supposed to be
us conning Marmalade.

1433
00:59:33,602 --> 00:59:36,761
It turns out
it was Wolf conning us.

1434
00:59:36,896 --> 00:59:38,438
(retching)

1435
00:59:38,574 --> 00:59:40,438
Does that sound familiar
to you, Wolf?

1436
00:59:40,574 --> 00:59:42,236
Why-why would you think that?

1437
00:59:42,371 --> 00:59:44,971
Oh, I don't know, maybe because
you just sabotaged

1438
00:59:45,106 --> 00:59:47,206
the biggest heist of our lives.

1439
00:59:47,341 --> 00:59:50,442
I think you owe us
an explanation, buddy.

1440
00:59:50,578 --> 00:59:51,875
(sighs)

1441
00:59:52,011 --> 00:59:53,119
Okay. You're right.

1442
00:59:53,254 --> 00:59:54,788
This is what happened.

1443
00:59:54,923 --> 00:59:57,448
Back in the museum, I just tried
to steal an old lady's purse.

1444
00:59:57,583 --> 00:59:59,423
-(camera shutter snaps)
-Classic snatch and grab.

1445
00:59:59,558 --> 01:00:01,758
Tried to? Since when do you try

1446
01:00:01,893 --> 01:00:03,763
to steal something
and not just steal it?

1447
01:00:03,898 --> 01:00:07,124
I was trying to steal the purse
when the old lady fell and...

1448
01:00:07,260 --> 01:00:09,234
(clears throat)
I kind of helped her.

1449
01:00:09,370 --> 01:00:10,267
-What?
-(camera shutter snaps)

1450
01:00:10,402 --> 01:00:12,362
I kind of helped her.

1451
01:00:12,498 --> 01:00:14,371
-But then you stole her purse.
-(camera shutter snaps)

1452
01:00:14,506 --> 01:00:15,804
(chuckling):
No, I didn't.

1453
01:00:15,939 --> 01:00:18,302
I saved the old lady,
and she hugged me,

1454
01:00:18,438 --> 01:00:20,939
and my tail wagged,
and I didn't know what it was,

1455
01:00:21,075 --> 01:00:24,449
but it felt, uh,
you know... good.

1456
01:00:24,584 --> 01:00:26,046
(Shark, Tarantula
and Piranha gasp)

1457
01:00:26,182 --> 01:00:27,217
Ah.

1458
01:00:27,353 --> 01:00:29,151
But then you stole the purse.

1459
01:00:29,286 --> 01:00:30,718
OTHERS:
No!

1460
01:00:30,854 --> 01:00:33,089
You know, I heard
what the pig said to you

1461
01:00:33,225 --> 01:00:34,783
about cutting us loose.

1462
01:00:34,919 --> 01:00:36,594
Wait. Like, "us" us?

1463
01:00:36,729 --> 01:00:38,687
But I never thought
you'd actually do it, man.

1464
01:00:38,823 --> 01:00:40,254
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

1465
01:00:40,389 --> 01:00:42,794
I-I would never...
I was trying to...

1466
01:00:42,929 --> 01:00:44,997
I was trying to find us
a better life.

1467
01:00:45,133 --> 01:00:48,597
Our life was perfect
until you decided to ruin it.

1468
01:00:48,732 --> 01:00:49,931
I didn't.

1469
01:00:50,067 --> 01:00:51,503
You guys felt it at the gala.

1470
01:00:51,638 --> 01:00:53,466
The clapping, the cheering.

1471
01:00:53,601 --> 01:00:55,867
We were more than...
than just scary villains.

1472
01:00:56,003 --> 01:00:57,105
They loved us.

1473
01:00:57,240 --> 01:00:59,671
Oh, yeah?
If they loved us so much,

1474
01:00:59,807 --> 01:01:03,408
how come we're in prison
for a crime we didn't commit?

1475
01:01:03,543 --> 01:01:05,684
You know what?
I'll give Marmalade this.

1476
01:01:05,820 --> 01:01:07,851
At least he sees the world
for what it is:

1477
01:01:07,986 --> 01:01:10,114
a place where
some people are scary

1478
01:01:10,249 --> 01:01:12,157
and some people are scared.

1479
01:01:12,292 --> 01:01:13,525
Oh, yeah?

1480
01:01:13,660 --> 01:01:15,220
Well, I'm tired of being scary.

1481
01:01:15,356 --> 01:01:16,923
I'm-I'm tired of
being an outcast.

1482
01:01:17,059 --> 01:01:18,657
Maybe I don't want to be a...

1483
01:01:18,792 --> 01:01:20,126
What? A Bad Guy?

1484
01:01:20,261 --> 01:01:22,298
Don't want to be
a Bad Guy anymore, huh?

1485
01:01:22,434 --> 01:01:24,538
Say it, Wolf.

1486
01:01:26,604 --> 01:01:28,065
Yeah, I thought so.

1487
01:01:28,201 --> 01:01:30,210
And us, your lifelong friends?

1488
01:01:30,345 --> 01:01:31,802
We're just holding you back?

1489
01:01:31,938 --> 01:01:33,744
Yeah, maybe you are!

1490
01:01:34,773 --> 01:01:35,972
(gasps)

1491
01:01:36,107 --> 01:01:37,714
(snarls) Take it back!

1492
01:01:37,849 --> 01:01:40,309
-(gasping)
-Take it back! Apologize!

1493
01:01:40,445 --> 01:01:42,177
GUARD:
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

1494
01:01:42,312 --> 01:01:43,812
Prison is no place for fighting.

1495
01:01:43,948 --> 01:01:45,280
(guard yells)

1496
01:01:45,415 --> 01:01:47,220
(groaning):
Tell that to him.

1497
01:01:47,356 --> 01:01:48,685
Huh?

1498
01:01:48,820 --> 01:01:50,859
♪ ♪

1499
01:01:52,831 --> 01:01:55,396
-(chuckling): What?
-(guards yelling)

1500
01:01:55,532 --> 01:01:57,766
(grunting, yelling)

1501
01:02:01,437 --> 01:02:03,373
(grunting rapidly)

1502
01:02:03,508 --> 01:02:05,939
(grunting and yelling continue)

1503
01:02:10,939 --> 01:02:11,939
(guard yelling)

1504
01:02:12,075 --> 01:02:13,649
-Shh.
-(grunts)

1505
01:02:15,750 --> 01:02:18,746
(grunting and yelling continue)

1506
01:02:19,215 --> 01:02:20,887
-(crunching)
-(grunting)

1507
01:02:24,591 --> 01:02:26,727
(screams, whimpers)

1508
01:02:29,595 --> 01:02:31,798
GUARD:
Run!

1509
01:02:34,862 --> 01:02:36,934
(groans)

1510
01:02:38,234 --> 01:02:39,805
-Oh!
-W-W-Wait, wait. Ho-Hold on.

1511
01:02:40,901 --> 01:02:42,065
(others gasping)

1512
01:02:42,200 --> 01:02:43,134
ALL:
Diane?

1513
01:02:43,270 --> 01:02:44,401
But how do you know how to do

1514
01:02:44,537 --> 01:02:45,710
all of that
kick-kick-punch-punch?

1515
01:02:45,846 --> 01:02:48,081
Wait a sec,
you're the Crimson Paw?

1516
01:02:48,216 --> 01:02:50,482
♪ ♪

1517
01:02:50,618 --> 01:02:52,077
WOLF:
<i>The queen of cons,</i>

1518
01:02:52,212 --> 01:02:53,476
<i>acrobatic Swiss Army knife.</i>

1519
01:02:53,611 --> 01:02:54,952
<i>Stole the Zumpango diamond</i>
<i>twice.</i>

1520
01:02:55,088 --> 01:02:57,455
<i>Once for profit,</i>
<i>second time just for fun.</i>

1521
01:02:57,590 --> 01:02:59,988
<i>Never identified, never caught.</i>

1522
01:03:00,124 --> 01:03:02,952
(chuckles) Guess I'm still
the best bad guy

1523
01:03:03,088 --> 01:03:04,960
the world has ever seen.

1524
01:03:05,095 --> 01:03:07,531
-Ugh, at least I used to be.
-(alarm blaring)

1525
01:03:07,666 --> 01:03:08,990
-(Shark gasps)
-TARANTULA: Huh?

1526
01:03:09,125 --> 01:03:11,934
(guards yelling)

1527
01:03:13,040 --> 01:03:14,436
(yells)

1528
01:03:14,572 --> 01:03:17,499
(explosions booming)

1529
01:03:18,334 --> 01:03:20,038
Nope, I'm still the best.

1530
01:03:20,174 --> 01:03:22,579
Just like riding
a stolen bicycle.

1531
01:03:22,715 --> 01:03:25,241
Oh, uh, you got a little...
Ouch.

1532
01:03:25,377 --> 01:03:27,443
Hey, wh-why did you
save us anyway?

1533
01:03:27,578 --> 01:03:29,676
After the gala,
I knew something wasn't right,

1534
01:03:29,811 --> 01:03:31,811
so I did some investigating,
and that meteor...

1535
01:03:31,947 --> 01:03:35,222
I know. Some kind of cosmic
mega-super-antennae thing.

1536
01:03:35,357 --> 01:03:38,058
Right. If conducted through
an array of ionized crystals,

1537
01:03:38,193 --> 01:03:40,053
it will generate a massive
psychokinetic field

1538
01:03:40,189 --> 01:03:41,388
the size of a city.

1539
01:03:41,524 --> 01:03:42,857
Oh, my gosh.
Did I interrupt you?

1540
01:03:42,993 --> 01:03:44,095
Were you gonna say that?

1541
01:03:44,230 --> 01:03:46,801
Uh, I-I-I was gonna be
a little more technical,

1542
01:03:46,936 --> 01:03:49,828
-but you got the gist of it.
-(chuckles)

1543
01:03:50,898 --> 01:03:54,039
Marmalade needs to be stopped,
but I can't do it alone.

1544
01:03:54,174 --> 01:03:56,276
You know his compound
better than anyone.

1545
01:03:56,412 --> 01:03:58,035
You can count on us.

1546
01:03:58,170 --> 01:03:59,345
Right, guys?

1547
01:03:59,480 --> 01:04:01,380
There is no "us."

1548
01:04:01,516 --> 01:04:03,040
We're through, Wolf.

1549
01:04:03,176 --> 01:04:04,576
Done. Finito.

1550
01:04:04,711 --> 01:04:07,047
Because of that little tiff
back there?

1551
01:04:07,182 --> 01:04:09,387
Come on, man, that's what we do.

1552
01:04:09,523 --> 01:04:11,081
You serve, I volley.

1553
01:04:11,217 --> 01:04:13,192
That's our little dance.

1554
01:04:13,328 --> 01:04:15,388
Not this time.

1555
01:04:18,299 --> 01:04:20,032
♪ ♪

1556
01:04:20,168 --> 01:04:21,558
Piranha?

1557
01:04:24,930 --> 01:04:26,138
Webs?

1558
01:04:26,274 --> 01:04:27,872
Sorry, Wolfie.

1559
01:04:29,642 --> 01:04:30,935
(chuckling):
Shark.

1560
01:04:31,070 --> 01:04:32,442
SHARK:
Hmm.

1561
01:04:32,577 --> 01:04:34,244
WOLF:
Hey.

1562
01:04:34,379 --> 01:04:35,945
Guys?

1563
01:04:36,908 --> 01:04:38,216
Guys?

1564
01:04:39,018 --> 01:04:42,545
You want to know why
I hate birthdays, Wolf? Do you?

1565
01:04:43,882 --> 01:04:47,649
When you grow up a snake,
nobody shows up to your party.

1566
01:04:47,785 --> 01:04:50,750
Birthdays are a constant
reminder that out there

1567
01:04:50,886 --> 01:04:55,898
I'm just a scary,
good-for-nothing monster.

1568
01:04:57,334 --> 01:04:59,000
Yeah.

1569
01:04:59,135 --> 01:05:01,935
But nothing compares
to having the one guy...

1570
01:05:02,070 --> 01:05:05,340
the one guy I thought
I could trust

1571
01:05:05,476 --> 01:05:07,568
stab me in the back.

1572
01:05:11,079 --> 01:05:13,750
Come on, guys.
Let's get out of here.

1573
01:05:22,017 --> 01:05:24,056
♪ ♪

1574
01:05:33,533 --> 01:05:35,099
(no audio)

1575
01:05:36,371 --> 01:05:38,597
♪ ♪

1576
01:05:42,277 --> 01:05:44,503
♪ ♪

1577
01:05:54,378 --> 01:05:57,080
(electrical crackling)

1578
01:05:57,215 --> 01:05:59,451
(rhythmic pulsing)

1579
01:06:00,819 --> 01:06:04,857
Now, this is what
a true bad guy looks like.

1580
01:06:04,992 --> 01:06:07,029
(electronic tone)

1581
01:06:10,902 --> 01:06:13,728
What do you say
we have some fun?

1582
01:06:16,573 --> 01:06:18,475
(rumbling)

1583
01:06:18,610 --> 01:06:19,707
(laughing maniacally)

1584
01:06:19,842 --> 01:06:22,637
(explosive whooshing)

1585
01:06:23,744 --> 01:06:25,776
(gasps, grunts)

1586
01:06:25,911 --> 01:06:28,148
(screams)

1587
01:06:32,016 --> 01:06:34,549
(chittering)

1588
01:06:38,725 --> 01:06:40,753
(screaming)

1589
01:06:42,731 --> 01:06:44,966
(squeaky chittering)

1590
01:06:52,640 --> 01:06:55,376
Hey. You okay?

1591
01:06:55,511 --> 01:06:57,136
No, I'm not okay.

1592
01:06:57,272 --> 01:06:59,972
I'm very, very un-okay.

1593
01:07:00,107 --> 01:07:01,144
(grumbles)

1594
01:07:01,280 --> 01:07:03,146
Just left the only friends
I have ever had,

1595
01:07:03,281 --> 01:07:06,612
so what am I... (sighs)
what am I doing?

1596
01:07:07,520 --> 01:07:09,279
(sighs)

1597
01:07:09,415 --> 01:07:12,217
I know this isn't easy,

1598
01:07:12,353 --> 01:07:14,492
leaving everything behind.

1599
01:07:14,627 --> 01:07:15,959
-Do you?
-Yeah.

1600
01:07:16,095 --> 01:07:18,420
I was the best thief
in the world.

1601
01:07:18,556 --> 01:07:22,427
Fast, fearless, inventive.

1602
01:07:22,563 --> 01:07:25,404
I just had one thing
left to steal.

1603
01:07:25,540 --> 01:07:27,164
The Golden Dolphin.

1604
01:07:27,299 --> 01:07:29,166
So you went after it.

1605
01:07:29,302 --> 01:07:31,173
I didn't just go after it.

1606
01:07:32,336 --> 01:07:34,238
<i>I had it.</i>

1607
01:07:34,374 --> 01:07:36,607
<i>And a clear escape route.</i>

1608
01:07:39,175 --> 01:07:41,150
<i>But...</i>

1609
01:07:41,285 --> 01:07:43,785
<i>all I saw in the end</i>
<i>was the tricky fox</i>

1610
01:07:43,920 --> 01:07:46,682
<i>that they always told me I was.</i>

1611
01:07:47,725 --> 01:07:49,925
<i>It changed everything.</i>

1612
01:07:50,060 --> 01:07:52,528
So, now,
instead of hurting people,

1613
01:07:52,664 --> 01:07:54,221
I'm helping them. (sighs)

1614
01:07:54,357 --> 01:07:55,928
I'm still me. (chuckles)

1615
01:07:56,064 --> 01:07:59,166
I'm just me on the right side.

1616
01:08:00,629 --> 01:08:02,104
You're doing the right thing.

1617
01:08:02,240 --> 01:08:05,706
And someday your friends,
if they're real friends,

1618
01:08:05,841 --> 01:08:08,042
I think they'll understand.

1619
01:08:08,911 --> 01:08:10,971
Now, come on, let's get inside.

1620
01:08:11,106 --> 01:08:13,942
-You look like you just busted
out of a prison. -(chuckles)

1621
01:08:14,077 --> 01:08:15,944
(both gasp)

1622
01:08:16,079 --> 01:08:17,350
(chitters)

1623
01:08:17,485 --> 01:08:18,816
-Guinea pigs? (gasps)
-(footsteps scurrying on roof)

1624
01:08:18,952 --> 01:08:20,277
BOTH:
Marmalade.

1625
01:08:20,413 --> 01:08:21,421
Let's bounce.

1626
01:08:21,556 --> 01:08:23,188
♪ ♪

1627
01:08:23,324 --> 01:08:25,959
So this is the hideout
of the great Crimson Paw.

1628
01:08:26,095 --> 01:08:27,361
-(Diane chuckles)
-(microwave beeping)

1629
01:08:27,496 --> 01:08:28,620
Snack break?

1630
01:08:28,755 --> 01:08:30,494
Okay, oddly timed,
but you do you.

1631
01:08:30,630 --> 01:08:31,688
(yells)

1632
01:08:31,823 --> 01:08:32,862
AUTOMATED VOICE:
Identity verified.

1633
01:08:32,998 --> 01:08:35,232
-What?
-Welcome, Diane.

1634
01:08:40,975 --> 01:08:44,040
-Whoa! Holy moly!
-(laughing)

1635
01:08:44,175 --> 01:08:46,478
(sighs)
It's so good to be home.

1636
01:08:46,614 --> 01:08:47,710
Are you kidding me?

1637
01:08:47,846 --> 01:08:49,474
Laser-sighted zip line?

1638
01:08:49,609 --> 01:08:52,180
The XM-2400 radar jammer?
No way.

1639
01:08:52,316 --> 01:08:54,453
I actually prefer
the earlier model.

1640
01:08:54,588 --> 01:08:56,347
Agree to disagree.

1641
01:08:56,482 --> 01:08:58,081
Uh, this stuff is nice, too.

1642
01:08:58,216 --> 01:08:59,249
(screams)

1643
01:08:59,385 --> 01:09:00,724
Yeah, that's a blowtorch.

1644
01:09:00,859 --> 01:09:02,853
Also, not really your color.

1645
01:09:02,989 --> 01:09:04,155
(groans)

1646
01:09:04,290 --> 01:09:05,964
All righty, Marmalade.

1647
01:09:06,099 --> 01:09:09,633
What are you up to,
you fuzzy little weirdo?

1648
01:09:09,769 --> 01:09:11,293
We need eyes on the city.

1649
01:09:11,429 --> 01:09:12,761
Let's see if we can't hack

1650
01:09:12,896 --> 01:09:14,169
into the government's
surveillance satellite.

1651
01:09:14,304 --> 01:09:16,037
But you're the governor.
Couldn't you just ask?

1652
01:09:16,173 --> 01:09:18,338
Yeah, but... (splutters)
the paperwork.

1653
01:09:19,468 --> 01:09:21,704
(Diane muttering)

1654
01:09:23,206 --> 01:09:26,981
I am definitely picking up
on suspicious activity here.

1655
01:09:27,117 --> 01:09:29,282
Those are guinea pig
heat signatures.

1656
01:09:29,417 --> 01:09:31,684
Marmalade seems to be
controlling them.

1657
01:09:31,819 --> 01:09:33,821
But to do what?

1658
01:09:33,957 --> 01:09:35,387
There are no obvious targets.

1659
01:09:37,389 --> 01:09:39,784
That's because
they're moving targets.

1660
01:09:39,919 --> 01:09:42,889
DIANE:
(gasps) His charity fundraiser.

1661
01:09:43,024 --> 01:09:45,296
He's gonna steal the money
raised in his own name?

1662
01:09:45,432 --> 01:09:47,965
It's the greatest heist
the world's ever seen.

1663
01:09:48,101 --> 01:09:50,137
$1 billion inside trucks,

1664
01:09:50,272 --> 01:09:52,270
on their way to charities
all over the city.

1665
01:09:52,406 --> 01:09:53,805
We need to cut off
Marmalade's communication

1666
01:09:53,941 --> 01:09:54,970
with his guinea pig army.

1667
01:09:55,106 --> 01:09:56,642
If there's no signal...

1668
01:09:56,777 --> 01:09:57,977
There's no heist.

1669
01:09:58,113 --> 01:10:00,206
BOTH:
We have to steal the meteorite.

1670
01:10:00,342 --> 01:10:01,444
That was very cute,

1671
01:10:01,579 --> 01:10:03,007
-that thing we just did there.
-All right.

1672
01:10:03,142 --> 01:10:05,517
Put on your big-girl pants.
We're gearing up.

1673
01:10:05,652 --> 01:10:08,219
♪ ♪

1674
01:10:11,517 --> 01:10:12,816
I wouldn't take that.

1675
01:10:12,952 --> 01:10:14,486
Those things rip your pants
right off.

1676
01:10:14,621 --> 01:10:16,319
Huh. Try wearing
clean underwear.

1677
01:10:16,455 --> 01:10:18,261
Just in case.

1678
01:10:19,224 --> 01:10:20,362
Wha...

1679
01:10:21,701 --> 01:10:23,961
You stole my car?

1680
01:10:24,097 --> 01:10:25,367
Respect.

1681
01:10:25,502 --> 01:10:28,139
-Let's do this.
-(engine revs, tires squeal)

1682
01:10:37,281 --> 01:10:39,440
-(elevator bell dings)
-(all gasp)

1683
01:10:39,575 --> 01:10:40,583
-No!
-What?

1684
01:10:40,719 --> 01:10:42,079
All our stuff?

1685
01:10:42,880 --> 01:10:44,384
-Where is everything?
-No, no, no, no, no.

1686
01:10:44,519 --> 01:10:46,186
-No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!
-All our stuff.

1687
01:10:46,322 --> 01:10:48,081
-It's all gone.
-My disguise closet!

1688
01:10:48,217 --> 01:10:50,456
-TARANTULA: Where's my things?
-(hangers clanging)

1689
01:10:51,555 --> 01:10:53,829
Wolf gave away all our loot.

1690
01:10:53,964 --> 01:10:56,261
We stole it fair and square.

1691
01:10:56,396 --> 01:10:58,398
Now I understand
what it feels like

1692
01:10:58,533 --> 01:11:01,162
to have things stolen from you.
(shuddering breaths)

1693
01:11:01,297 --> 01:11:03,004
I don't like it!

1694
01:11:03,139 --> 01:11:05,833
I really don't like it!
(whimpers)

1695
01:11:09,605 --> 01:11:11,209
-(groans)
-(Shark sobbing)

1696
01:11:11,345 --> 01:11:13,839
SHARK: We got no food.
We got no money.

1697
01:11:13,975 --> 01:11:15,378
We got no money
we could use to buy food.

1698
01:11:15,514 --> 01:11:17,485
No food we can sell for money.
(grunts)

1699
01:11:17,620 --> 01:11:19,687
We... (sobs)

1700
01:11:19,822 --> 01:11:21,886
All right, okay, okay.

1701
01:11:22,022 --> 01:11:24,283
Here, here. Take it.

1702
01:11:24,419 --> 01:11:26,458
Now, stop crying, buddy.

1703
01:11:26,594 --> 01:11:28,293
(sighs)

1704
01:11:29,161 --> 01:11:33,798
Um, Snake, what did you just do?

1705
01:11:33,934 --> 01:11:35,592
What? My friend was sad.

1706
01:11:35,727 --> 01:11:37,165
I was just cheering him up.

1707
01:11:37,300 --> 01:11:39,664
You... you did a good thing.

1708
01:11:39,799 --> 01:11:41,666
-For me.
-Don't be ridiculous.

1709
01:11:41,802 --> 01:11:43,999
I just put your needs
before my own.

1710
01:11:44,134 --> 01:11:46,510
-Yeah. You're being good.
-I'm not.

1711
01:11:46,645 --> 01:11:49,543
I was simply making a sacrifice
so Shark could be happy.

1712
01:11:49,678 --> 01:11:52,682
That is the actual definition
of being good.

1713
01:11:52,817 --> 01:11:54,712
Snake, you,

1714
01:11:54,848 --> 01:11:56,953
the worst one of us,
the most selfish.

1715
01:11:57,088 --> 01:11:58,548
-Spiteful.
-Terrible.

1716
01:11:58,683 --> 01:11:59,781
-Sneaky.
-Dishonest.

1717
01:11:59,917 --> 01:12:00,957
-Insensitive.
-Manipulative.

1718
01:12:01,092 --> 01:12:02,450
-Snakelike.
-Stanky.

1719
01:12:02,585 --> 01:12:04,485
And your point is?

1720
01:12:04,621 --> 01:12:06,394
I think Wolf was right.

1721
01:12:06,530 --> 01:12:09,529
Maybe we could be more
than just scary villains.

1722
01:12:10,536 --> 01:12:12,026
(gasps)

1723
01:12:12,967 --> 01:12:14,001
Wh...?

1724
01:12:14,136 --> 01:12:15,838
TARANTULA:
Oh, wow.

1725
01:12:15,973 --> 01:12:18,471
Is this... is this wagging?

1726
01:12:19,470 --> 01:12:21,137
We're-we're wagging.

1727
01:12:21,272 --> 01:12:22,809
(grunting)

1728
01:12:22,944 --> 01:12:25,638
No, no, no!

1729
01:12:25,774 --> 01:12:29,877
We'll always be Bad Guys!

1730
