1982
01:23:04,737 --> 01:23:06,238
WOLF:
Take the wheel.

1983
01:23:06,373 --> 01:23:07,530
Not so fast.

1984
01:23:07,666 --> 01:23:10,968
Pull him up first,
or I'll use this.

1985
01:23:11,104 --> 01:23:12,910
Oh, come now.

1986
01:23:15,238 --> 01:23:16,845
(chuckling)

1987
01:23:16,980 --> 01:23:19,675
Do it, or you'll lose the rock.

1988
01:23:20,717 --> 01:23:22,152
If you insist.

1989
01:23:22,288 --> 01:23:23,646
Cuddles!

1990
01:23:30,596 --> 01:23:33,021
You want him? He's yours.

1991
01:23:33,156 --> 01:23:35,166
(grunts, yells)

1992
01:23:35,301 --> 01:23:37,092
(screaming)

1993
01:23:37,227 --> 01:23:39,335
Snake! No, no, no!

1994
01:23:39,471 --> 01:23:41,336
-Snake!
-Oh, no!

1995
01:23:41,472 --> 01:23:43,173
(engine revs)

1996
01:23:43,308 --> 01:23:45,699
♪ ♪

1997
01:23:50,546 --> 01:23:52,947
(screaming)

1998
01:23:54,578 --> 01:23:57,217
Guys, I know it's crazy,
but we're gonna jump it.

1999
01:23:57,352 --> 01:24:00,222
Crazy? You're finally speaking
my language,<i> chico.</i>

2000
01:24:00,357 --> 01:24:02,792
(engine revving)

2001
01:24:08,221 --> 01:24:10,397
♪ ♪

2002
01:24:10,533 --> 01:24:13,802
We're gonna make it!

2003
01:24:14,702 --> 01:24:15,962
TARANTULA:
No!

2004
01:24:16,097 --> 01:24:19,206
(all screaming)

2005
01:24:19,341 --> 01:24:21,131
(wind whistling)

2006
01:24:21,267 --> 01:24:22,975
You came back.

2007
01:24:23,972 --> 01:24:25,772
(grunting)

2008
01:24:25,907 --> 01:24:26,977
Snake.

2009
01:24:27,112 --> 01:24:28,471
I should've been honest
with you.

2010
01:24:28,607 --> 01:24:29,816
I was afraid that if you knew

2011
01:24:29,951 --> 01:24:31,576
I-I wanted to be good
that you'd...

2012
01:24:31,711 --> 01:24:34,618
Act like a jerk
and never talk to you again?

2013
01:24:34,754 --> 01:24:36,412
(laughing):
Yeah.

2014
01:24:36,547 --> 01:24:38,524
Point is I... I-I-I, you know...

2015
01:24:38,660 --> 01:24:41,223
Yeah. I love you, too, buddy.

2016
01:24:45,456 --> 01:24:47,129
This-this is so beautiful.

2017
01:24:47,265 --> 01:24:49,665
Do you know how beautiful
this is, you guys?

2018
01:24:49,801 --> 01:24:50,898
-(Shark sobbing)
-Now...

2019
01:24:51,034 --> 01:24:52,734
Now you're gonna make me cry.

2020
01:24:52,869 --> 01:24:54,372
(sobbing):
I know!

2021
01:24:54,508 --> 01:24:55,966
So pathetic, right?

2022
01:24:56,102 --> 01:24:58,034
Come on, guys.

2023
01:24:58,170 --> 01:24:59,842
Who said it was the end?

2024
01:24:59,977 --> 01:25:01,245
-(all gasp)
-(Shark chuckles)

2025
01:25:01,380 --> 01:25:03,644
♪ ♪

2026
01:25:03,780 --> 01:25:06,015
(all whooping, laughing)

2027
01:25:10,312 --> 01:25:12,020
(chittering)

2028
01:25:13,685 --> 01:25:15,656
MARMALADE: No, no, no, don't...
No, no. Cuddles!

2029
01:25:15,791 --> 01:25:17,421
We're losing altitude!

2030
01:25:17,556 --> 01:25:19,753
We're losing altitude!
We're going down!

2031
01:25:24,467 --> 01:25:25,930
(groans, coughs)

2032
01:25:26,066 --> 01:25:27,962
What happened? Did we blow up?

2033
01:25:28,097 --> 01:25:30,037
Is this heaven?

2034
01:25:32,068 --> 01:25:34,107
(grunting)

2035
01:25:38,881 --> 01:25:40,744
CHIEF (chuckles):
That is it.

2036
01:25:40,879 --> 01:25:42,380
PIRANHA:
Hey!

2037
01:25:42,516 --> 01:25:45,544
There is absolutely no way
you're getting away this time.

2038
01:25:45,680 --> 01:25:47,588
-Wait, Chief.
-Governor Foxington?

2039
01:25:47,724 --> 01:25:48,919
-Don't do this.
-WOLF: Ow!

2040
01:25:49,054 --> 01:25:50,348
They didn't steal the meteorite.

2041
01:25:50,483 --> 01:25:51,657
They were bringing it back.

2042
01:25:51,792 --> 01:25:53,783
Ha! How could you know that?

2043
01:25:53,918 --> 01:25:56,827
Unless...
unless you were conspiring

2044
01:25:56,962 --> 01:25:59,559
with a bunch of known criminals.

2045
01:26:00,492 --> 01:26:02,435
Well... (clears throat)

2046
01:26:02,571 --> 01:26:04,935
as a matter of fact,

2047
01:26:05,071 --> 01:26:07,297
it's time I came clean
about something.

2048
01:26:08,100 --> 01:26:11,404
The truth is I'm really...
(clears throat) r-really...

2049
01:26:11,539 --> 01:26:14,005
Really a big fan
of redemption arcs.

2050
01:26:14,141 --> 01:26:15,871
Yeah, we know.

2051
01:26:19,715 --> 01:26:21,177
(mews)

2052
01:26:21,313 --> 01:26:22,552
We're done running away.

2053
01:26:22,687 --> 01:26:23,652
-Yeah.
-Mm-hmm.

2054
01:26:23,788 --> 01:26:25,480
-Yeah.
-Yep.

2055
01:26:25,616 --> 01:26:27,489
Chief, do what you need to do.

2056
01:26:27,624 --> 01:26:28,725
What?

2057
01:26:28,861 --> 01:26:31,619
Y-You're turning yourself in?

2058
01:26:31,755 --> 01:26:33,555
We might not have stolen
the meteorite,

2059
01:26:33,691 --> 01:26:36,031
but we did steal
a lot of other things.

2060
01:26:36,167 --> 01:26:38,567
It's time we took
some responsibility.

2061
01:26:38,703 --> 01:26:40,861
Start a clean state.

2062
01:26:41,672 --> 01:26:43,599
Take us in, Chief.

2063
01:26:44,398 --> 01:26:45,837
Wow, really?

2064
01:26:45,973 --> 01:26:47,269
You finally did it.

2065
01:26:47,404 --> 01:26:48,608
This is your moment, Chief.

2066
01:26:48,743 --> 01:26:49,972
Drink it in.

2067
01:26:50,107 --> 01:26:51,244
(gasps) Wow.

2068
01:26:51,379 --> 01:26:52,705
You know, I should...
I should give a speech.

2069
01:26:52,841 --> 01:26:53,981
I... Well, I-I should,
shouldn't I?

2070
01:26:54,117 --> 01:26:55,815
-Uh... (mutters)
-(chief clears throat)

2071
01:26:55,950 --> 01:26:57,249
When I was six years old,

2072
01:26:57,384 --> 01:26:59,019
I decided that I wanted
to play the piccolo,

2073
01:26:59,155 --> 01:27:00,979
only to find that
my fingers were just

2074
01:27:01,114 --> 01:27:03,816
too powerful for that
fragile little instrument.

2075
01:27:03,951 --> 01:27:06,423
And that's when I discovered
law enforcement.

2076
01:27:06,558 --> 01:27:07,957
-(chuckles)
-(chief continues indistinctly)

2077
01:27:08,093 --> 01:27:09,756
I'm proud of you, Wolf.

2078
01:27:09,891 --> 01:27:13,099
You know, a fox and a wolf
are not that different.

2079
01:27:13,234 --> 01:27:15,166
You got a good thing
going here, Governor.

2080
01:27:15,302 --> 01:27:17,434
So, it turns out the saga
of the Bad Guys

2081
01:27:17,570 --> 01:27:21,074
has come to a simple and
totally satisfying conclusion.

2082
01:27:21,210 --> 01:27:23,909
Though I wonder,
what happened to the meteorite?

2083
01:27:24,044 --> 01:27:25,834
MARMALADE:
Cuddles! Faster, faster!

2084
01:27:25,970 --> 01:27:27,539
TIFFANY:
It's Professor Marmalade!

2085
01:27:27,675 --> 01:27:29,773
He's bringing
the meteorite back.

2086
01:27:29,909 --> 01:27:32,410
-Huh? Uh, yes, yes.
-(crowd clamoring)

2087
01:27:32,546 --> 01:27:34,413
Bringing... bringing it back.

2088
01:27:34,548 --> 01:27:36,285
That's precisely
what I am doing.

2089
01:27:39,691 --> 01:27:41,626
Look no further.

2090
01:27:41,761 --> 01:27:43,926
Your hero has arrived.

2091
01:27:44,061 --> 01:27:45,488
Professor, care to comment?

2092
01:27:45,624 --> 01:27:47,261
I tried to help them, Tiffany,

2093
01:27:47,397 --> 01:27:50,063
but in the end,
it's the same old story.

2094
01:27:50,199 --> 01:27:53,097
Bad guys bad, good guys good.

2095
01:27:53,232 --> 01:27:54,730
So true. So wise.

2096
01:27:54,866 --> 01:27:56,305
Furthermore,
for the good of the city,

2097
01:27:56,440 --> 01:27:58,943
I have generously decided
to take the meteorite

2098
01:27:59,078 --> 01:28:01,774
back to my compound
for safekeeping.

2099
01:28:01,909 --> 01:28:03,178
(cheering)

2100
01:28:03,313 --> 01:28:04,912
Is he seriously gonna
get away with this?

2101
01:28:05,048 --> 01:28:07,583
Thank you. Gosh, you're kind.

2102
01:28:07,718 --> 01:28:09,510
Give it up for me!

2103
01:28:09,645 --> 01:28:10,983
CHIEF:
Wait a second.

2104
01:28:11,119 --> 01:28:12,779
This isn't the meteorite.

2105
01:28:12,915 --> 01:28:14,491
-It's a lamp.
-(Marmalade gasps)

2106
01:28:14,626 --> 01:28:15,748
ALL:
Huh?

2107
01:28:15,884 --> 01:28:17,356
-(Snake chuckling)
-OTHERS: What?

2108
01:28:17,491 --> 01:28:19,653
TARANTULA:
<i>Snake, what did you just do?</i>

2109
01:28:19,788 --> 01:28:21,488
SNAKE:
<i>What? My friend was sad,</i>

2110
01:28:21,623 --> 01:28:22,755
<i>and I was just cheering him up.</i>

2111
01:28:22,891 --> 01:28:24,398
TARANTULA:
<i>I think Wolf was right.</i>

2112
01:28:24,533 --> 01:28:27,667
<i>Maybe we could be more</i>
<i>than just scary villains.</i>

2113
01:28:27,802 --> 01:28:30,038
♪ ♪

2114
01:28:30,839 --> 01:28:32,398
I'm bad. You're bad.

2115
01:28:32,533 --> 01:28:33,873
Let's be bad together.

2116
01:28:34,008 --> 01:28:36,242
You've got yourself a deal.

2117
01:28:37,741 --> 01:28:40,613
-Can I try it on?
-Of course, partner.

2118
01:28:40,748 --> 01:28:42,973
♪ ♪

2119
01:28:55,260 --> 01:28:56,958
-(Marmalade gasps)
-Don't mind us.

2120
01:28:57,094 --> 01:28:58,456
Just robbing this place.

2121
01:28:58,591 --> 01:29:00,726
(engine revs, tires squeal)

2122
01:29:02,768 --> 01:29:04,763
No, no, no!

2123
01:29:08,471 --> 01:29:10,234
But if that's a lamp,
where is the...

2124
01:29:10,369 --> 01:29:11,367
(Snake chuckling)

2125
01:29:11,503 --> 01:29:12,742
The old switcheroo.

2126
01:29:12,878 --> 01:29:14,277
(whirring, rumbling)

2127
01:29:15,247 --> 01:29:17,412
-(explosive whooshing)
-(officers gasp)

2128
01:29:23,754 --> 01:29:25,947
(wind whistles)

2129
01:29:31,894 --> 01:29:34,095
♪ ♪

2130
01:29:34,230 --> 01:29:36,429
-(car engine starts)
-(purring)

2131
01:29:37,965 --> 01:29:40,367
(siren wailing)

2132
01:29:42,464 --> 01:29:44,239
It's a butt.

2133
01:29:45,075 --> 01:29:47,307
(object whistling through air)

2134
01:29:48,568 --> 01:29:49,903
(whimpers)

2135
01:29:51,011 --> 01:29:52,209
CHIEF:
Hold on.

2136
01:29:52,345 --> 01:29:54,607
This is the Zumpango diamond.

2137
01:29:54,743 --> 01:29:56,549
But this was stolen by the...

2138
01:29:56,685 --> 01:29:58,048
(gasps)

2139
01:29:58,184 --> 01:30:00,577
By the Crimson Paw.

2140
01:30:00,713 --> 01:30:02,114
Me? Oh, oh, no, no, no.

2141
01:30:02,250 --> 01:30:04,017
-OMG. -MARMALADE: No, no, no.
No, you've got it wrong.

2142
01:30:04,152 --> 01:30:05,984
-And a shocking twist.
-You're making a huge mistake!

2143
01:30:06,119 --> 01:30:09,393
The notorious bandit
known as the Crimson Paw

2144
01:30:09,528 --> 01:30:11,132
-has been revealed to be...
-No! No!

2145
01:30:11,267 --> 01:30:12,791
...none other
than Professor Marmalade.

2146
01:30:12,926 --> 01:30:14,156
MARMALADE:
I'm not the Crimson Paw.

2147
01:30:14,292 --> 01:30:15,932
-Sh-She's the Crimson Paw.
-(sirens wailing)

2148
01:30:16,067 --> 01:30:17,628
Sh-She's the Paw!

2149
01:30:17,764 --> 01:30:19,764
I'm a flower of goodness. No!

2150
01:30:19,900 --> 01:30:21,967
Ooh! That's my reptile
right there.

2151
01:30:22,102 --> 01:30:23,836
-That's what I'm talking about!
All right! -Yeah!

2152
01:30:23,972 --> 01:30:26,108
Come on, somebody had to
destroy that meteorite.

2153
01:30:26,243 --> 01:30:28,079
That thing was dangerous.

2154
01:30:28,215 --> 01:30:30,077
That was pretty good there,
Snakey.

2155
01:30:30,213 --> 01:30:32,444
Good? It was genius.

2156
01:30:32,579 --> 01:30:34,286
Not only did I foil the pig,

2157
01:30:34,421 --> 01:30:36,951
I got you to admit
how much you care about me.

2158
01:30:37,086 --> 01:30:38,354
Sure, yeah.

2159
01:30:38,490 --> 01:30:40,088
I just wonder about
one little thing.

2160
01:30:40,223 --> 01:30:41,623
Oh, yeah? What's that, Wolf?

2161
01:30:41,759 --> 01:30:45,955
Who do you think put that
one Push Pop in the fridge?

2162
01:30:47,391 --> 01:30:48,698
Wait.

2163
01:30:48,833 --> 01:30:50,361
You... No.

2164
01:30:50,496 --> 01:30:51,835
I knew you were good.

2165
01:30:51,971 --> 01:30:54,234
-(laughter)
-No.

2166
01:30:54,369 --> 01:30:57,171
-We good, baby. We good.
-Yeah!

2167
01:30:57,306 --> 01:31:00,303
♪ You feelin' all right? ♪

2168
01:31:00,438 --> 01:31:02,344
♪ Uh-huh ♪

2169
01:31:02,479 --> 01:31:05,879
♪ I'm not feelin'
too good myself ♪

2170
01:31:06,014 --> 01:31:08,181
♪ Uh-huh ♪

2171
01:31:08,316 --> 01:31:11,654
♪ Yeah, you feelin' all right? ♪

2172
01:31:11,789 --> 01:31:13,321
♪ Uh-huh ♪

2173
01:31:13,456 --> 01:31:16,791
♪ I'm not feelin'
too good, little girl ♪

2174
01:31:16,926 --> 01:31:19,150
♪ Uh-huh ♪

2175
01:31:20,690 --> 01:31:22,754
♪ Seems I've got to have ♪

2176
01:31:22,889 --> 01:31:26,031
♪ A change of scene ♪

2177
01:31:26,167 --> 01:31:28,231
♪ Every night, I have ♪

2178
01:31:28,367 --> 01:31:30,436
♪ The strangest dreams ♪

2179
01:31:31,404 --> 01:31:33,830
♪ Imprisoned by the way ♪

2180
01:31:33,965 --> 01:31:36,474
♪ It could have been ♪

2181
01:31:37,738 --> 01:31:39,011
♪ Left here on my own ♪

2182
01:31:39,146 --> 01:31:41,480
♪ Or so it seems... ♪

2183
01:31:41,616 --> 01:31:44,017
WOLF:<i> Okay, so imagine</i>
<i>it's your birthday.</i>

2184
01:31:44,152 --> 01:31:45,516
SNAKE:
It is my birthday.

2185
01:31:45,651 --> 01:31:47,182
WOLF: Yeah, I know.
So, but we're walking along

2186
01:31:47,317 --> 01:31:48,680
and you meet a genie.

2187
01:31:48,816 --> 01:31:50,151
SNAKE:
Okay. What's his name?

2188
01:31:50,287 --> 01:31:51,521
What's the genie's name?

2189
01:31:51,656 --> 01:31:53,158
Yeah, I want to know
who I'm talking to.

2190
01:31:53,294 --> 01:31:54,685
I don't know,
Genie or Gene for short.

2191
01:31:54,821 --> 01:31:56,354
So he offers you three wishes.

2192
01:31:56,489 --> 01:31:57,523
Why three?

2193
01:31:57,658 --> 01:31:58,786
You know, industry standard.

2194
01:31:58,922 --> 01:32:00,197
Now, what do you wish for?

2195
01:32:00,332 --> 01:32:01,965
-Uh...
-Good luck out there, guys.

2196
01:32:02,101 --> 01:32:03,462
I'm gonna go with nothing.

2197
01:32:03,597 --> 01:32:04,760
(laughing):
Nothing?

2198
01:32:04,895 --> 01:32:06,337
Come on, it's your birthday.

2199
01:32:06,472 --> 01:32:08,465
All right,
but what do I need wishes for?

2200
01:32:08,600 --> 01:32:10,038
I got my freedom.

2201
01:32:10,174 --> 01:32:11,106
-Hey.
-Guys!

2202
01:32:11,242 --> 01:32:12,472
Looking good,<i> hermanos.</i>

2203
01:32:12,607 --> 01:32:14,377
-I got my friends.
-TARANTULA: Aw.

2204
01:32:14,512 --> 01:32:16,380
I got the skin of a reptile
half my age.

2205
01:32:16,515 --> 01:32:18,808
I don't know about half
your age, but you do look good.

2206
01:32:18,944 --> 01:32:20,284
Well, that's because
you just molted.

2207
01:32:20,419 --> 01:32:22,516
-Yes, I did.
-SHARK: You smell good, too.

2208
01:32:22,652 --> 01:32:26,080
-I'm shiny. I'm gorgeous.
-(laughter)

2209
01:32:31,887 --> 01:32:34,855
Uh, so what do we do now?

2210
01:32:34,990 --> 01:32:36,765
-Steal a car?
-Piranha!

2211
01:32:36,901 --> 01:32:38,557
I was joking.

2212
01:32:38,693 --> 01:32:40,025
It was a joke.

2213
01:32:40,160 --> 01:32:41,762
You know,
on second thought, Wolf,

2214
01:32:41,897 --> 01:32:43,930
maybe I'd, uh, wish for a ride.

2215
01:32:44,066 --> 01:32:46,139
-Oh, yeah? Alakazam.
-(snaps fingers)

2216
01:32:46,274 --> 01:32:48,272
(engine revs, tires squeal)

2217
01:32:48,407 --> 01:32:49,707
-Nice.
-(laughter)

2218
01:32:49,842 --> 01:32:52,672
-Hey, guys.
Ready to get to work? -(mews)

2219
01:32:52,808 --> 01:32:53,980
(chuckling):
Hey. Whoa.

2220
01:32:54,115 --> 01:32:55,976
TARANTULA:
Aw.

2221
01:32:56,776 --> 01:32:58,686
(engine revs)

2222
01:32:58,821 --> 01:33:00,018
Hey, you.

2223
01:33:00,154 --> 01:33:01,513
That's right. Come here.

2224
01:33:01,649 --> 01:33:02,789
Little closer.

2225
01:33:02,925 --> 01:33:04,490
I said closer.

2226
01:33:04,626 --> 01:33:07,817
Now that we've had some time
to get acquainted, uh,

2227
01:33:07,953 --> 01:33:10,455
not so scary now, are we?

2228
01:33:10,591 --> 01:33:11,957
Webs, hit it.

2229
01:33:12,093 --> 01:33:13,964
("Brand New Day" by The Heavy
playing)

2230
01:33:14,100 --> 01:33:15,692
(engine revs)

2231
01:33:15,828 --> 01:33:17,963
(laughter, whooping)

2232
01:33:24,342 --> 01:33:28,740
